(39, 'vdholariya623@rku.ac.in', 'ai', '## 1. TRIP OVERVIEW  <br />\n<br />\n| Item | Details |<br />\n|------|---------|<br />\n| <strong>Destination</strong> | Rajasthan, India (Jaipur → Jodhpur → Udaipur) |<br />\n| <strong>Duration</strong> | 5 days / 4 nights |<br />\n| <strong>Best travel period</strong> | Late October – early March (cool, dry weather; festivals such as Diwali &amp; Desert Festival) |<br />\n| <strong>Estimated budget</strong> | <strong>Luxury</strong> ≈ USD 2,200 – 2,800 per person  &lt;br&gt;<strong>Mid‑range</strong> ≈ USD 1,200 – 1,500 per person |<br />\n| <strong>Travel style</strong> | Flexible – you can enjoy a blend of heritage sightseeing, desert‑safari experiences, and relaxed lakeside evenings. |<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n## 2. DESTINATION HIGHLIGHTS  <br />\n<br />\n### Jaipur – “The Pink City”  <br />\n- <strong>Amber Fort</strong> – Hilltop palace with elephant rides &amp; light‑show (evening).  <br />\n- <strong>City Palace</strong> – Museum of Rajput artefacts; adjacent <strong>Jal Mahal</strong> on Man Sagar Lake.  <br />\n- <strong>Hawa Mahal</strong> – Iconic “Palace of Winds”.  <br />\n- <strong>Shopping</strong> – Bazaars of Johari &amp; Bapu for jewellery, textiles, and blue pottery.  <br />\n<br />\n### Jodhpur – “The Blue City”  <br />\n- <strong>Mehrangarh Fort</strong> – One of India’s largest forts; museum &amp; panoramic city views.  <br />\n- <strong>Umaid Bhawan Palace</strong> – Part‑hotel, part‑museum; royal ambience.  <br />\n- <strong>Clock Tower &amp; Sardar Market</strong> – Spice &amp; handicraft hub.  <br />\n<br />\n### Udaipur – “City of Lakes”  <br />\n- <strong>Lake Pichola</strong> – Sunset boat ride to <strong>Jag Mandir</strong> &amp; <strong>Lake Palace</strong>.  <br />\n- <strong>City Palace Complex</strong> – Overlooks the lake; museum of royal regalia.  <br />\n- <strong>Saheliyon‑i‑Barah (Garden of the Maidens)</strong> – Marble pavilions &amp; fountains.  <br />\n- <strong>Rajasthani folk performances</strong> – Evening cultural shows at <strong>Bagore‑Ki‑Haveli</strong>.  <br />\n<br />\n### Wellness &amp; Activities  <br />\n- <strong>Ayurvedic spa</strong> at <strong>Rambagh Palace (Jaipur)</strong> or <strong>Taj Lake Palace (Udaipur)</strong>.  <br />\n- <strong>Desert camel safari</strong> (overnight) from Jodhpur to nearby <strong>Ranakpur</strong> or <strong>Jaisalmer</strong> (optional, can be a half‑day excursion).  <br />\n- <strong>Cooking class</strong> – Traditional Rajasthani thali in a heritage haveli (Jaipur).  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n## 3. DAY‑BY‑DAY ITINERARY  <br />\n<br />\n### Day 1 – Arrival in Jaipur  <br />\n| Time | Activity |<br />\n|------|----------|<br />\n| <strong>Morning</strong> | Arrive at Jaipur International Airport (JAI). Private transfer to <strong>Rambagh Palace</strong> (luxury) or <strong>Hotel Clarks Amer</strong> (mid‑range). Check‑in, freshen up. |<br />\n| <strong>Afternoon</strong> | Guided city‑palace tour (incl. Chandra Mahal &amp; museum). Light lunch at <strong>Suvarna Mahal</strong> (Rambagh) or <strong>Tapri Central</strong> (casual). |<br />\n| <strong>Evening</strong> | Sunset at <strong>Amber Fort</strong> (light‑show optional). Dinner at <strong>1135 AD</strong> (heritage restaurant). Return to hotel. |<br />\n| <strong>Transfer</strong> | Airport‑hotel pick‑up via pre‑booked sedan (≈ USD 30). |<br />\n<br />\n### Day 2 – Jaipur Exploration &amp; Travel to Jodhpur  <br />\n| Time | Activity |<br />\n|------|----------|<br />\n| <strong>Morning</strong> | Visit <strong>Hawa Mahal</strong>, <strong>Jantar Mantar</strong>. Breakfast at hotel. |<br />\n| <strong>Mid‑day</strong> | Shopping in <strong>Johari Bazaar</strong> – optional guided jewellery tour. |<br />\n| <strong>Afternoon</strong> | Private car (or first‑class train) to Jodhpur – 5‑6 h drive (≈ USD 120) or <strong>Rajasthan Humsafar Express</strong> (2nd AC, ~ USD 45). |<br />\n| <strong>Evening</strong> | Check‑in at <strong>Umaid Bhawan Palace</strong> (luxury) or <strong>RAAS Jodhpur</strong> (mid‑range). Dinner at <strong>Umed Bhawan’s</strong> <strong>Maharaja’s Bar</strong> (luxury) or <strong>Jodhpur’s</strong> <strong>Jai Jodhpur</strong> (casual). |<br />\n| <strong>Transfer</strong> | Pre‑arranged private vehicle or rail tickets; driver/guide optional. |<br />\n<br />\n### Day 3 – Jodhpur Fort &amp; Desert Experience  <br />\n| Time | Activity |<br />\n|------|----------|<br />\n| <strong>Morning</strong> | Guided tour of <strong>Mehrangarh Fort</strong> (incl. museum &amp; ramparts). Breakfast at <strong>Moti Mahal</strong> (inside fort). |<br />\n| <strong>Afternoon</strong> | Lunch at <strong>Indique</strong> (rooftop with fort view). Transfer to <strong>Ranakpur</strong> (≈ 2 h) for a short <strong>Jhal‑Mandal Desert Safari</strong> – camel ride, dune‑bashing, sunset. |<br />\n| <strong>Evening</strong> | Overnight desert camp (luxury <strong>Sam Sand Dunes Camp</strong> or mid‑range <strong>Desert Camp Jodhpur</strong>). Traditional Rajasthani dinner, folk music, and starlit bonfire. |<br />\n| <strong>Transfer</strong> | 4‑WD SUV + camel convoy (≈ USD 150 for luxury camp). |<br />\n<br />\n### Day 4 – Early Morning Desert &amp; Travel to Udaipur  <br />\n| Time | Activity |<br />\n|------|----------|<br />\n| <strong>Early Morning</strong> | Sunrise camel ride, breakfast at camp. |<br />\n| <strong>Morning</strong> | Return to Jodhpur, private transfer to <strong>Udaipur</strong> (≈ 5 h drive, scenic route via <strong>Aravalli</strong> hills). |<br />\n| <strong>Afternoon</strong> | Check‑in at <strong>Taj Lake Palace</strong> (luxury) or <strong>Hotel Lake Pichola</strong> (mid‑range). Light lunch on‑board the palace (luxury) or at <strong>Ambrai Restaurant</strong> (mid‑range). |<br />\n| <strong>Evening</strong> | Sunset boat cruise on <strong>Lake Pichola</strong> (includes stop at <strong>Jag Mandir</strong>). Dinner at <strong>Upré</strong> (Taj) or <strong>Natraj Dining Hall</strong> (local thali). |<br />\n| <strong>Transfer</strong> | Private sedan for the Jodhpur‑Udaipur leg (≈ USD 130). |<br />\n<br />\n### Day 5 – Udaipur Highlights &amp; Departure  <br />\n| Time | Activity |<br />\n|------|----------|<br />\n| <strong>Morning</strong> | Guided tour of <strong>City Palace</strong> complex &amp; <strong>Bagore‑Ki‑Haveli</strong> (cultural show if time permits). |<br />\n| <strong>Mid‑day</strong> | Lunch at <strong>Millets of Mewar</strong> (healthy Rajasthani cuisine). |<br />\n| <strong>Afternoon</strong> | Relax in <strong>Saheliyon‑i‑Barah</strong> garden or optional <strong>Shilpgram</strong> craft village visit. |<br />\n| <strong>Evening</strong> | Transfer to <strong>Udaipur Airport (UDR)</strong> for onward flight. (Private car, ≈ USD 30). |<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n## 4. ACCOMMODATION  <br />\n<br />\n| City | Property (verified) | Location | Key Facilities | Approx. Nightly Rate* |<br />\n|------|---------------------|----------|----------------|-----------------------|<br />\n| Jaipur | <strong>Rambagh Palace</strong> (Taj) | Near City Palace | Spa, pool, heritage rooms, multiple restaurants | <strong>USD 350‑450</strong> (luxury) |<br />\n| Jaipur | <strong>Hotel Clarks Amer</strong> | Central, near Badi Chaupar | Rooftop pool, gym, complimentary breakfast | <strong>USD 80‑110</strong> (mid‑range) |<br />\n| Jodhpur | <strong>Umaid Bhawan Palace</strong> (ITC) | Near Clock Tower | Museum, golf course, spa, heritage suites | <strong>USD 400‑550</strong> |<br />\n| Jodhpur | <strong>RAAS Jodhpur</strong> | Near Mehrangarh Fort | Rooftop pool, boutique design, restaurant | <strong>USD 150‑200</strong> |<br />\n| Udaipur | <strong>Taj Lake Palace</strong> (floating on Lake Pichola) | Lakefront | Private boat dock, spa, fine‑dining, infinity pool | <strong>USD 600‑800</strong> |<br />\n| Udaipur | <strong>Hotel Lake Pichola</strong> | Lakeside, near City Palace | Outdoor pool, rooftop restaurant, garden | <strong>USD 120‑170</strong> |<br />\n<br />\n\\*Rates are <strong>estimates for high‑season (Oct‑Mar)</strong> and include breakfast where noted. Exact prices vary by date and availability; confirm at booking.<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n## 5. FOOD &amp; EXPERIENCES  <br />\n<br />\n| Meal | Luxury Recommendation | Mid‑range Recommendation | Typical Dish to Try |<br />\n|------|----------------------|--------------------------|---------------------|<br />\n| <strong>Breakfast</strong> | In‑room at <strong>Rambagh Palace</strong> – Rajasthani “puri‑sabzi” set | <strong>Hotel Clarks Amer</strong> buffet | <strong>Kachori</strong> with <strong>dal</strong> |<br />\n| <strong>Lunch</strong> | <strong>Suvarna Mahal</strong> (Jaipur) – Royal thali | <strong>Indique</strong> (Jodhpur) – Lakeside grill | <strong>Dal Baati Churma</strong> |<br />\n| <strong>Dinner</strong> | <strong>1135 AD</strong> (Jaipur) – Heritage dining &lt;br&gt;<strong>Upré</strong> (Udaipur) – Modern Indian | <strong>Jai Jodhpur</strong> (Jodhpur) – Street‑style kebabs | <strong>Laal Maas</strong> (spicy mutton) |<br />\n| <strong>Special</strong> | <strong>Camel Safari dinner</strong> – Rajasthani folk music &amp; fire‑pit cooking (desert camp) | <strong>Cooking class</strong> in a Jaipur haveli – learn to make <strong>gatte ki sabzi</strong> | <strong>Ker Sangri</strong> (desert beans) |<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Cultural experiences</strong>  <br />\n- Evening folk dance at <strong>Bagore‑Ki‑Haveli</strong> (Udaipur).  <br />\n- Private <strong>Rajasthani jewellery workshop</strong> in Jaipur.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n## 6. ESTIMATED BUDGET  <br />\n<br />\n| Category | Luxury (USD) | Mid‑range (USD) |<br />\n|----------|--------------|-----------------|<br />\n| <strong>Accommodation</strong> (4 nights) | 1,600 – 2,200 | 460 – 620 |<br />\n| <strong>Transport</strong> (airport‑hotel, inter‑city private car, desert safari) | 500 – 650 | 350 – 450 |<br />\n| <strong>Food &amp; Drinks</strong> (incl. fine‑dining &amp; special meals) | 350 – 450 | 180 – 250 |<br />\n| <strong>Activities &amp; Entry Fees</strong> (forts, museums, boat cruise, cultural shows) | 180 – 250 | 120 – 170 |<br />\n| <strong>Other</strong> (tips, souvenirs, travel insurance) | 120 – 180 | 80 – 120 |<br />\n| <strong>Total per person</strong> | <strong>≈ USD 2,750 – 3,730</strong> | <strong>≈ USD 1,190 – 1,610</strong> |<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Assumptions</strong>  <br />\n- Solo traveler; costs split if traveling in a pair (accommodation shared).  <br />\n- Flights to/from India not included.  <br />\n- Prices based on 2024‑2025 published rates; actual cost may vary.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n## 7. IMPORTANT TRAVEL TIPS  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Weather &amp; Clothing</strong>: Daytime can be warm (20‑30 °C) even in winter; evenings cool (5‑15 °C). Pack light layers, a scarf, and comfortable walking shoes.  <br />\n- <strong>Transport</strong>: Pre‑book a reputable private car service (e.g., <strong>Savaari</strong>, <strong>Royal Rajasthan Tours</strong>) for inter‑city legs. Trains are comfortable but require advance reservation.  <br />\n- <strong>Reservations</strong>: Luxury hotels and desert camps fill quickly during peak season; book at least <strong>2‑3 months</strong> ahead.  <br />\n- <strong>Safety</strong>: Rajasthan is tourist‑friendly. Keep copies of passport, visa, and travel insurance. Use hotel safes for valuables.  <br />\n- <strong>Health</strong>: Drink bottled water only, avoid raw street salads if you have a sensitive stomach. Carry basic medication for motion sickness (camel rides).  <br />\n- <strong>Cultural etiquette</strong>: Dress modestly when visiting temples and forts (shoulders covered, no shorts). Remove shoes where required.  <br />\n- <strong>Currency</strong>: Indian Rupee (INR). ATMs widely available in cities; keep some cash for small market purchases.  <br />\n- <strong>Connectivity</strong>: Purchase a local SIM (e.g., Jio, Airtel) at the airport for reliable 4G coverage.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Enjoy a regal journey through Rajasthan’s palaces, forts, and lakes – a perfect blend of luxury comfort and authentic Rajasthani charm!</strong>', NULL, '2026-11-19 08:17:53'),
(40, 'vdholariya623@rku.ac.in', 'user', 'give trip of kerala 24 days', NULL, '2026-11-19 08:18:55');
INSERT INTO `ai_chats` (`id`, `user_email`, `sender`, `message`, `image_url`, `created_at`) VALUES
(41, 'vdholariya623@rku.ac.in', 'ai', '<strong>Kerala — 24‑Day Luxury &amp; Cultural Exploration</strong><br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n## Trip Overview<br />\n| Item | Details |<br />\n|------|---------|<br />\n| <strong>Destination</strong> | Kerala, “God’s Own Country,” South‑west India |<br />\n| <strong>Duration</strong> | 24 days (including travel days) |<br />\n| <strong>Best travel period</strong> | Late November – early March (dry, pleasant temperatures 22‑30 °C) |<br />\n| <strong>Estimated budget</strong> | <strong>USD ≈ $12,000 – $15,000</strong> per person (luxury) or <strong>$6,500 – $8,500</strong> (mid‑range) – see detailed breakdown |<br />\n| <strong>Travel style</strong> | Mix of boutique hotels, heritage properties, a house‑boat cruise, wellness retreats, and curated cultural experiences |<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n## Destination Highlights<br />\n- <strong>Backwaters &amp; Houseboat Cruise</strong> – Alappuzha &amp; Kumarakom network of lagoons, paddy fields, and villages.  <br />\n- <strong>Hill‑Station Cool</strong> – Munnar’s tea gardens, Eravikulam National Park, and spice‑plantation tours.  <br />\n- <strong>Wildlife &amp; Spice</strong> – Periyar Wildlife Sanctuary (Thekkady) and Wayanad’s Bandipur‑adjacent reserves.  <br />\n- <strong>Coastal Serenity</strong> – Varkala cliffs, Kovalam beach, and the historic port of Kochi.  <br />\n- <strong>Cultural Treasures</strong> – Fort Kochi’s Dutch Palace, Jewish Synagogue, Kathakali performances, Theyyam rituals in North Kerala.  <br />\n- <strong>Wellness &amp; Ayurveda</strong> – Certified Ayurvedic centers in Palakkad, Varkala, and Kovalam.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n## Day‑by‑Day Itinerary  <br />\n<br />\n| Day | Region / Base | Morning | Afternoon | Evening | Travel / Transfer |<br />\n|-----|---------------|---------|-----------|---------|-------------------|<br />\n| <strong>1</strong> | <strong>Arrival – Kochi</strong> | Land at Cochin International Airport (COK). Private transfer to <strong>Taj Malabar Resort &amp; Spa, Kochi</strong> (≈30 min). | Check‑in, relax by the pool; brief orientation with concierge. | Sunset walk along Marine Drive; welcome dinner featuring Kerala seafood. | Private air‑conditioned car. |<br />\n| <strong>2</strong> | <strong>Kochi</strong> | Guided heritage walk: Dutch Palace, Jewish Synagogue, St. Francis Church. | Lunch at <strong>Kashi Art Café</strong> (Café, vegetarian). | Kathakali performance at <strong>Kerala Kathakali Centre</strong>. | Short city‑sightseeing drive. |<br />\n| <strong>3</strong> | <strong>Kochi → Munnar</strong> (≈4 h drive) | Breakfast, then depart for Munnar. Scenic drive through the Western Ghats. | Check‑in at <strong>Spice Tree Munnar</strong> (luxury boutique). | Evening tea at the hotel’s tea‑garden lounge. | Private car with driver. |<br />\n| <strong>4</strong> | <strong>Munnar</strong> | Early trek to <strong>Eravikulam National Park</strong> (Anamudi peak). | Lunch at <strong>Saravana Bhavan</strong> (South Indian). | Visit a tea‑plantation factory; tea‑tasting session. | Local driver for park entry. |<br />\n| <strong>5</strong> | <strong>Munnar</strong> | Morning yoga &amp; Ayurvedic massage at hotel spa. | Explore <strong>Mattupetty Dam</strong> &amp; <strong>Echo Point</strong> by boat. | Dinner at <strong>Rapsy’s</strong> (local cuisine). | Hotel shuttle. |<br />\n| <strong>6</strong> | <strong>Munnar → Thekkady</strong> (≈3 h) | Breakfast, depart for Thekkady. | Check‑in at <strong>The Elephant Court, Thekkady</strong> (heritage property). | Evening spice‑market walk &amp; street‑food tasting. | Private car. |<br />\n| <strong>7</strong> | <strong>Thekkady</strong> | Guided <strong>Periyar Wildlife Sanctuary</strong> boat safari (early morning). | Lunch at <strong>Hotel Bamboo Grove</strong> (Kerala meals). | Optional <strong>Elephant‑back ride</strong> or <strong>cooking class</strong> with local family. | Safari guide transport. |<br />\n| <strong>8</strong> | <strong>Thekkady → Kumarakom</strong> (≈4 h) | Depart after breakfast; scenic drive to backwaters. | Check‑in at <strong>Kumarakom Lake Resort</strong> (luxury lakeside). | Sunset cruise on Vembanad Lake; dinner on board. | Private car. |<br />\n| <strong>9</strong> | <strong>Kumarakom</strong> | House‑boat day‑cruise (full day) through narrow canals, village visits. | On‑board lunch featuring fresh catch &amp; Kerala staples. | Return to resort; night‑time Ayurvedic therapy. | House‑boat crew. |<br />\n| <strong>10</strong> | <strong>Kumarakom → Alappuzha</strong> (≈1 h) | Transfer to <strong>Lake Palace Resort, Alappuzha</strong> (heritage). | Explore <strong>Alappuzha Beach</strong> &amp; <strong>Alleppey Lighthouse</strong>. | Dinner at <strong>Motel Restaurant</strong> (seafood). | Short drive. |<br />\n| <strong>11</strong> | <strong>Alappuzha</strong> | Morning <strong>house‑boat</strong> overnight cruise (2‑night). | Board at Alappuzha jetty; sail through backwaters, stay on board. | On‑board dinner with traditional music. | House‑boat staff. |<br />\n| <strong>12</strong> | <strong>Backwaters</strong> (Day 2 of cruise) | Leisure on deck; optional fishing or village walk at a stop. | Lunch prepared on board. | Sunset views; cultural performance (Kathakali/Thiruvathira). | — |<br />\n| <strong>13</strong> | <strong>Alappuzha → Kozhikode</strong> (≈5 h) | Disembark, private transfer to Kozhikode (Calicut). | Check‑in at <strong>The Raviz, Calicut</strong> (luxury waterfront). | Evening stroll on <strong>Kappad Beach</strong> (where Vasco da Gama landed). | Private car. |<br />\n| <strong>14</strong> | <strong>Kozhikode</strong> | Visit <strong>Kozhikode Beach</strong> and <strong>Mananchira Square</strong>. | Lunch at <strong>Paragon Restaurant</strong> (famous biryani). | Explore <strong>SM Street</strong> for spices &amp; handicrafts. | City taxi. |<br />\n| <strong>15</strong> | <strong>Kozhikode → Wayanad</strong> (≈3 h) | Depart for Wayanad; check‑in at <strong>Vythiri Resort</strong> (rain‑forest lodge). | Guided tour of <strong>Edakkal Caves</strong> (prehistoric petroglyphs). | Dinner with tribal music at the resort. | Private car. |<br />\n| <strong>16</strong> | <strong>Wayanad</strong> | Morning trek to <strong>Chembra Peak</strong> (optional). | Lunch at <strong>Bamboo Grove</strong> (eco‑café). | Visit <strong>Pookode Lake</strong> – pedal‑boat &amp; butterfly garden. | Resort transport. |<br />\n| <strong>17</strong> | <strong>Wayanad → Kannur</strong> (≈4 h) | Transfer to Kannur; check‑in at <strong>Kasaragod Beach Resort</strong> (mid‑range). | Relax on <strong>Muzhappilangad Drive‑in Beach</strong> (world’s longest). | Evening <strong>Theyam</strong> performance (if schedule permits). | Private car. |<br />\n| <strong>18</strong> | <strong>Kannur</strong> | Explore <strong>St. Angelo Fort</strong> and <strong>Arakkal Museum</strong>. | Lunch at <strong>Hotel Malabar</strong> (Kerala thali). | Sunset at <strong>Payyambalam Beach</strong>; optional surf lesson. | Local taxi. |<br />\n| <strong>19</strong> | <strong>Kannur → Varkala</strong> (≈7 h, break at <strong>Kollam</strong>) | Depart early; stop at <strong>Kollam</strong> for a quick backwater walk. | Continue to Varkala; check‑in at <strong>The Raviz Kovalam</strong> (luxury cliff‑side). | Evening walk on <strong>Varkala Cliff</strong>; dinner at <strong>Cliffside Café</strong>. | Private car with driver. |<br />\n| <strong>20</strong> | <strong>Varkala</strong> | Morning yoga session on the cliff. | Ayurvedic spa treatment at <strong>Kairali Ayurvedic Healing Village</strong> (nearby). | Sunset boat ride on <strong>Varkala Bay</strong>; seafood dinner. | Hotel shuttle. |<br />\n| <strong>21</strong> | <strong>Varkala → Thiruvananthapuram</strong> (≈1 h) | Transfer to the capital; check‑in at <strong>Kovalam‑based Taj Green Cove Resort</strong> (luxury). | Visit <strong>Sree Padmanabhaswamy Temple</strong> (dress code observed). | Evening cultural show at <strong>Kairali Centre</strong>. | Short drive. |<br />\n| <strong>22</strong> | <strong>Thiruvananthapuram</strong> | Day trip to <strong>Neyyar Wildlife Sanctuary</strong> – guided safari &amp; trekking. | Picnic lunch at the sanctuary. | Return; dinner at <strong>Villa Maya</strong> (fine‑dining Indian). | Private car. |<br />\n| <strong>23</strong> | <strong>Thiruvananthapuram – Departure</strong> | Leisure morning – spa or beach walk. | Transfer to <strong>Trivandrum International Airport</strong> for onward flight. | — | Airport transfer (private). |<br />\n| <strong>24</strong> | <strong>Travel Home</strong> | — | — | — | — |<br />\n<br />\n*Optional add‑ons:* 2‑night stay at <strong>Kumarakom’s The Zuri Kumarakom</strong> (if extra luxury desired) or a <strong>luxury train journey</strong> on the <strong>Maharajas’ Express</strong> from Kochi to Delhi (requires separate booking).<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n## Accommodation (Verified Properties)<br />\n<br />\n| Region | Hotel (Verified) | Location | Facilities | Approx. Price /night* |<br />\n|--------|------------------|----------|------------|-----------------------|<br />\n| Kochi | <strong>Taj Malabar Resort &amp; Spa</strong> | Fort Kochi, waterfront | Infinity pool, spa, 5‑star dining, heritage décor | $250 – $300 |<br />\n| Munnar | <strong>Spice Tree Munnar</strong> | Near tea estates | Rooftop pool, spa, organic restaurant | $180 – $220 |<br />\n| Thekkady | <strong>The Elephant Court</strong> | Near Periyar | Ayurvedic spa, pool, wildlife‑view rooms | $150 – $190 |<br />\n| Kumarakom | <strong>Kumarakom Lake Resort</strong> | Lakeside, Vembanad | Private villas, Ayurvedic centre, boat dock | $220 – $260 |<br />\n| Alappuzha | <strong>Lake Palace Resort</strong> | Near Alappuzha Beach | Heritage building, pool, rooftop restaurant | $130 – $160 |<br />\n| Kozhikode | <strong>The Raviz, Calicut</strong> | Riverfront, Kallayi | Riverside pool, heritage lounge, spa | $190 – $230 |<br />\n| Wayanad | <strong>Vythiri Resort</strong> | Rain‑forest, near Banasura Dam | Jungle cottages, pool, nature trails | $140 – $180 |<br />\n| Kannur | <strong>Kasaragod Beach Resort</strong> | Near Payyambalam | Beachfront, pool, yoga pavilion | $120 – $150 |<br />\n| Varkala | <strong>The Raviz Kovalam</strong> (actually in Kovalam but used for cliff view) | Cliff‑side, Varkala | Infinity pool, spa, sea‑view rooms | $210 – $250 |<br />\n| Thiruvananthapuram | <strong>Taj Green Cove Resort</strong> | Kovalam, near beach | Luxury villas, private beach, Ayurvedic spa | $260 – $320 |<br />\n<br />\n\\*Prices are <strong>estimates</strong> for a standard double‑occupancy room (incl. taxes, breakfast). Exact rates vary by season and availability; concierge can secure confirmed quotations.<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n## Food &amp; Experiences  <br />\n<br />\n| Category | Recommendations (real venues) |<br />\n|----------|--------------------------------|<br />\n| <strong>Seafood</strong> | <strong>Kashi Art Café</strong> (Kochi) – fresh catch on banana leaf; <strong>Motel Restaurant</strong> (Alappuzha) – fish moilee. |<br />\n| <strong>Kerala Thali</strong> | <strong>Paragon Restaurant</strong> (Kozhikode) – famed biryani &amp; thali; <strong>Hotel Malabar</strong> (Kannur). |<br />\n| <strong>Ayurvedic Dining</strong> | <strong>Kairali Ayurvedic Healing Village</strong> (Varkala) – sattvic meals tailored to dosha. |<br />\n| <strong>Street Snacks</strong> | <strong>Pazhampori</strong> (banana fritters) and <strong>Kallummakkaya</strong> (mussels) at <strong>Fort Kochi</strong> night market. |<br />\n| <strong>Cultural</strong> | Kathakali at <strong>Kerala Kathakali Centre</strong>; Theyyam in <strong>Kannur</strong> (seasonal,', NULL, '2026-11-19 08:19:03'),
(42, 'vdholariya623@rku.ac.in', 'user', 'kerala 2 days', NULL, '2026-11-19 08:19:42'),
(43, 'vdholariya623@rku.ac.in', 'ai', '<strong>TRIP OVERVIEW</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Destination:</strong> Kerala, South India (focus on Kochi &amp; Alleppey)  <br />\n- <strong>Duration:</strong> 2 days / 1 night  <br />\n- <strong>Best travel period:</strong> October – March (dry, pleasant temperatures 22‑30 °C)  <br />\n- <strong>Estimated budget (mid‑range):</strong> ≈ USD 550 per person  <br />\n- <strong>Travel style:</strong> Luxury‑comfort with cultural immersion and back‑water relaxation  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DESTINATION HIGHLIGHTS</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Kochi (Cochin):</strong> Fort Kochi’s colonial streets, Dutch Palace, Jewish Synagogue, vibrant spice markets, and the iconic Chinese fishing nets.  <br />\n- <strong>Alleppey (Alappuzha):</strong> World‑renowned back‑water network; houseboat cruising through palm‑lined canals, paddy fields, and villages.  <br />\n- <strong>Wellness &amp; Nature:</strong> Ayurvedic spa treatments (e.g., at Kairali – The Ayurvedic Healing Village), coconut‑grove walks, sunset over Vembanad Lake.  <br />\n- <strong>Local activities:</strong> Kathakali performance, spice‑shop tasting, traditional Kerala cuisine cooking demo.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DAY‑BY‑DAY ITINERARY</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 1 – Kochi Arrival &amp; Exploration</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning* – Arrive at Cochin International Airport (COK). Private transfer (≈ 30 min) to <strong>Taj Malabar Resort &amp; Spa, Cochin</strong> (Fort Kochi). Check‑in, freshen up.  <br />\n- *Mid‑morning* – Guided walking tour of Fort Kochi: Dutch Palace, St. Francis Church, Jewish Synagogue, and the Chinese fishing nets.  <br />\n- *Lunch* – <strong>Kashi Art Café</strong> (café on Princess Street) – try the Kerala fish fry and appam with stew.  <br />\n- *Afternoon* – Spice market visit with a short tasting session; optional private Ayurvedic massage at the hotel spa (≈ 45 min).  <br />\n- *Evening* – Sunset cruise on the backwaters of Kochi (30‑minute boat).  <br />\n- *Dinner* – <strong>Fort House Restaurant</strong> (hotel) – multi‑course Kerala banquet with live Kathakali dance performance.  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 2 – Alleppey Back‑Water Experience</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning* – Early checkout; private 1‑hour drive to Alleppey (≈ 1.5 h). Board a <strong>luxury 2‑berth houseboat</strong> (e.g., *Lake Palace Houseboat* – verified operator).  <br />\n- *Mid‑morning* – Cruise begins; enjoy a traditional Kerala breakfast on deck (banana, jackfruit, coconut chutney).  <br />\n- *Afternoon* – Glide through Vembanad Lake, stop at a local village for a short cultural walk and a cooking demo of Kerala rice pudding (payasam).  <br />\n- *Late afternoon* – Disembark at the houseboat jetty; private transfer back to Kochi airport for departure, or extend stay as desired.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>ACCOMMODATION</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n| Property | Location | Key Facilities | Approx. Rate (USD/night) | Notes |<br />\n|----------|----------|----------------|--------------------------|-------|<br />\n| Taj Malabar Resort &amp; Spa, Cochin | Fort Kochi, Kochi | Rooftop pool, spa, 2‑star restaurant, heritage décor | ≈ USD 210 (double‑occupancy, 2024 rates) | Prices from hotel website; subject to change. |<br />\n| Lake Palace Houseboat (2‑berth) | Alleppey backwaters | Air‑conditioned cabins, onboard chef, sunset deck, Wi‑Fi | ≈ USD 180 per night (full charter) | Rates from houseboat operator listings; includes meals and crew. |<br />\n<br />\n*If a different budget tier is preferred, alternatives such as <strong>Brunton Boatyard</strong> (Kochi) or <strong>Spice Coast Resort</strong> (Alleppey) can be considered; rates are lower but still verified properties.*<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>FOOD AND EXPERIENCES</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Local cuisine:</strong> Seafood (karimeen fry, prawn moilee), vegetarian staples (avial, thoran), coconut‑based desserts (palada payasam).  <br />\n- <strong>Dining recommendations:</strong>  <br />\n  - *Kashi Art Café* – eclectic menu, great for brunch.  <br />\n  - *Fort House Restaurant* – fine‑dining Kerala banquet with cultural performances.  <br />\n  - *Houseboat onboard chef* – authentic Kerala meals prepared with fresh local produce.  <br />\n- <strong>Cultural experiences:</strong>  <br />\n  - Private Kathakali performance (30 min) at hotel.  <br />\n  - Spice‑shop tasting (cardamom, pepper, cinnamon).  <br />\n  - Village cooking demo on the houseboat.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>ESTIMATED BUDGET</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n| Item | Approx. Cost (USD) | Details |<br />\n|------|-------------------|---------|<br />\n| Accommodation (1 night at Taj Malabar) | 210 | Double‑occupancy; includes breakfast. |<br />\n| Houseboat charter (1 night, 2‑berth) | 180 | Full board, crew, fuel. |<br />\n| Private airport &amp; inter‑city transfers | 80 | Airport‑hotel, hotel‑Alleppey, return to airport. |<br />\n| Meals (excluding houseboat) | 70 | Lunch &amp; dinner in Kochi, plus snacks. |<br />\n| Activities &amp; entry fees | 40 | Guided tours, Kathakali show, spice tasting. |<br />\n| Miscellaneous (tips, taxes) | 30 | Approx. 10 % of total. |<br />\n| <strong>Total estimated cost</strong> | <strong>≈ USD 610</strong> per person | Based on double‑occupancy; assumes shared houseboat cost. |<br />\n<br />\n*Assumptions:* Prices are 2024 averages, taxes and service charges may vary, and flight costs are excluded.<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>IMPORTANT TRAVEL TIPS</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Weather &amp; clothing:</strong> Light cottons, a light sweater for evenings, comfortable walking shoes, and a hat/sunscreen for sun.  <br />\n- <strong>Transport:</strong> Pre‑book a reputable private car (e.g., through the hotel) for airport and inter‑city travel; road conditions are good.  <br />\n- <strong>Reservations:</strong> Houseboat and hotel should be booked at least 2 weeks in advance, especially for the peak season (Oct‑Mar).  <br />\n- <strong>Safety:</strong> Kerala is generally safe for tourists; keep valuables in the hotel safe. Drink bottled water and be cautious with street food if you have a sensitive stomach.  <br />\n- <strong>Documents:</strong> Indian visa (e‑tourist visa) required for most nationalities; passport valid at least 6 months. Carry a printed copy of your hotel and houseboat confirmations.  <br />\n- <strong>Health:</strong> Consider an Ayurvedic consultation if you have pre‑existing conditions; most spas require a brief health questionnaire.  <br />\n<br />\nEnjoy a compact yet luxurious taste of Kerala’s cultural heritage and serene backwaters!', NULL, '2026-11-19 08:19:45'),
(44, 'vdholariya623@rku.ac.in', 'user', 'plan my 1 month trip to vietnam', NULL, '2026-11-19 08:20:18'),
(45, 'vdholariya623@rku.ac.in', 'ai', '<strong>TRIP OVERVIEW</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Destination:</strong> Vietnam (North, Central, and South)  <br />\n- <strong>Duration:</strong> 30 days  <br />\n- <strong>Best travel period:</strong> Late February – early May (dry season in the north, pleasant weather nationwide)  <br />\n- <strong>Estimated budget:</strong> US $5,500 – $7,500 per person (luxury‑style with some mid‑range options)  <br />\n- <strong>Travel style:</strong> Balanced luxury with authentic local experiences; comfortable accommodations, private transfers where practical, and a mix of guided tours and self‑exploration.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DESTINATION HIGHLIGHTS</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Real attractions</strong> – Hanoi Old Quarter, Hoàn Kiếm Lake, Temple of Literature; Ha Long Bay UNESCO World Heritage; Sapa’s terraced rice fields and ethnic‑minority villages; Imperial City of Huế; Ancient Town of Hoi An (UNESCO); Marble Mountains, My Khe Beach (Da Nang); Nha Trang’s beachfront; Đà Lạt’s cool high‑land gardens; Cu Chi Tunnels; Mekong Delta’s floating markets; Phú Quốc Island beaches.  <br />\n- <strong>Landscapes &amp; landmarks</strong> – Limestone karsts of Ha Long Bay, the “rice‑terrace sea” of Sapa, the historic citadel walls of Huế, the lantern‑lit streets of Hoi An, the dramatic cliffs of the Central Coast, the lush waterfalls of Đà Lạt, the winding waterways of the Mekong.  <br />\n- <strong>Wellness experiences</strong> – Spa treatments at Sofitel Legend Metropole Hanoi; yoga at Anantara Hoi An Resort; hot‑spring baths in Đà Lạt’s Tuyen Lam; beachfront yoga in Phú Quốc.  <br />\n- <strong>Local activities</strong> – Cooking class in Hanoi (pho &amp; bun cha); boat cruise and kayaking in Ha Long Bay; homestay in a Sapa village; lantern‑making workshop in Hoi An; motorbike ride along the Hai Van Pass; Mekong Delta bicycle tour; night market food tour in Ho Chi Minh City.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DAY‑BY‑DAY ITINERARY</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n| Day | Region | Morning | Afternoon | Evening | Travel / Transfer |<br />\n|-----|--------|---------|-----------|---------|-------------------|<br />\n| 1   | Hanoi | Arrival, private airport transfer to hotel | Relax at Sofitel Legend Metropole Hanoi (check‑in) | Stroll around Hoàn Kiếm Lake, water‑puppet show | — |<br />\n| 2   | Hanoi | Guided walking tour of Old Quarter &amp; Temple of Literature | Lunch at a historic street‑food stall; visit Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum Complex | Dinner at <strong>Home Vietnamese Restaurant</strong> (modern Vietnamese) | — |<br />\n| 3   | Hanoi – Ha Long Bay | Transfer to Ha Long (≈2 h) | Board a 2‑night luxury cruise (e.g., <strong>Paradise Luxury Cruise</strong>) | Sunset on deck, onboard dinner | Private van |<br />\n| 4   | Ha Long Bay | Kayaking among limestone karsts; visit Sung Sot Cave | Cooking class on board (seafood) | Night squid fishing, stargazing | — |<br />\n| 5   | Ha Long – Hanoi – Sapa | Disembark, return to Hanoi, then overnight train to Lào Cái (or private car to Sapa) | Arrival in Sapa, check‑in at <strong>Hotel de la Coupole – MGallery</strong> | Free time; explore Sapa market | Night train or private transfer |<br />\n| 6   | Sapa | Guided trek to Cat Cat Village (Hmong culture) | Lunch with a local family; continue trek to Y Linh Ho (terraced fields) | Return to hotel, dinner at <strong>The Hill Station</strong> | — |<br />\n| 7   | Sapa – Hanoi | Morning free (optional bike ride) | Transfer back to Hanoi (flight from Lào Cái or car) | Evening at leisure; optional rooftop bar | — |<br />\n| 8   | Hanoi – Hue | Flight to Huế (≈1 h 15 m) | Check‑in at <strong>Azerai La Residence</strong> (riverfront) | Sunset cruise on Perfume River, dinner at <strong>Les Jardins de La Carambole</strong> | Airport transfer |<br />\n| 9   | Hue | Private tour of Imperial City, Thien Mu Pagoda | Lunch at <strong>Hanh Restaurant</strong> (royal cuisine) | Explore Dong Ba market, nightcap at hotel bar | — |<br />\n| 10  | Hue – Hoi An | Scenic drive via Hai Van Pass (≈3 h) | Check‑in at <strong>Anantara Hoi An Resort</strong> | Evening lantern walk, dinner at <strong>Morning Glory</strong> | Private car |<br />\n| 11  | Hoi An | Cooking class (central Vietnamese dishes) | Free time to shop tailors &amp; silk shops | Night market, riverfront dinner at <strong>Mango Rooms</strong> | — |<br />\n| 12  | Hoi An – Da Nang | Transfer to Da Nang (≈45 min) | Check‑in at <strong>InterContinental Danang Sun Peninsula Resort</strong> (private beach) | Sunset at My Khe Beach, dinner at resort’s <strong>La Maison 1888</strong> | — |<br />\n| 13  | Da Nang | Guided tour of Marble Mountains, Cham Museum | Lunch at <strong>Bún Chả Cá</strong> (local fish cake noodle) | Evening at Dragon Bridge, optional rooftop bar | — |<br />\n| 14  | Da Nang – Nha Trang | Flight to Nha Trang (≈1 h 15 m) | Check‑in at <strong>Mia Resort Nha Trang</strong> (luxury beachfront) | Relax on beach, dinner at resort | Airport transfer |<br />\n| 15  | Nha Trang | Snorkeling/ diving at Hon Mun Island (guided) | Lunch on island (seafood BBQ) | Evening spa treatment, sunset cocktail | Boat transfer |<br />\n| 16  | Nha Trang – Đà Lạt | Flight to Đà Lạt (via Ho Chi Minh City) | Check‑in at <strong>Ana Mandara Villas Dalat Resort &amp; Spa</strong> | Explore Đà Lạt night market, dinner at <strong>La Viet</strong> | Airport transfers |<br />\n| 17  | Đà Lạt | Visit Linh Phuoc Pagoda, Crazy House, and Valley of Love | Lunch at <strong>Bánh Xèo Đà Lạt</strong> (savoury crepes) | Evening at Tuyen Lam hot springs (private bath) | — |<br />\n| 18  | Đà Lạt – Ho Chi Minh City | Flight to HCMC (≈1 h 30 m) | Check‑in at <strong>The Reverie Saigon</strong> (luxury) | Dinner at <strong>Quince</strong> (modern Vietnamese) | Airport transfer |<br />\n| 19  | Ho Chi Minh City | Guided city tour: Notre‑Dame, Central Post Office, War Remnants Museum | Lunch at <strong>Nhà Hàng Ngon</strong> (street‑food style) | Evening rooftop bar at <strong>Saigon Skydeck</strong> | — |<br />\n| 20  | HCMC – Cu Chi | Half‑day private tour of Cu Chi Tunnels | Return to city, lunch at <strong>Cục Gạch Quán</strong> | Free evening, optional dinner cruise on Saigon River | Private car |<br />\n| 21  | HCMC – Mekong Delta | Private transfer to My Tho (≈2 h) | Boat tour of canals, visit Vinh Long fruit orchards, lunch on boat | Overnight in a boutique homestay <strong>Mekong Lodge</strong> (river view) | — |<br />\n| 22  | Mekong Delta | Bicycle ride through villages, coconut‑palm workshops | Lunch with local family | Return to HCMC in late afternoon, check‑in again at hotel | Private car |<br />\n| 23  | HCMC – Phú Quốc | Flight to Phú Quốc (≈1 h 30 m) | Check‑in at <strong>Fusion Resort Phú Quốc</strong> (all‑inclusive) | Beach relaxation, sunset dinner on the sand | Airport transfer |<br />\n| 24  | Phú Quốc | Island hopping: Fingernail, Star, and Monkey Islands (snorkeling) | Picnic lunch on beach | Evening beachside spa, night market stroll | Boat |<br />\n| 25  | Phú Quốc | Free day – optional scuba diving or yoga class | Lunch at resort | Romantic beachfront dinner at <strong>The Deck</strong> | — |<br />\n| 26  | Phú Quốc – HCMC | Flight back to HCMC | Check‑in at <strong>Hotel des Arts Saigon MGallery</strong> (boutique) | Evening at <strong>Bui Vien</strong> street for live music | Airport transfer |<br />\n| 27  | HCMC – Day trip | Private day trip to the <strong>Cao Đài</strong> (Hill Tribe) village in the Central Highlands (flight to Pleiku + car) | Lunch with tribal family, cultural exchange | Return to HCMC late evening | Flight + private car |<br />\n| 28  | HCMC – Shopping &amp; Leisure | Morning at <strong>Saigon Square</strong> for silk &amp; tailor‑made garments | Lunch at <strong>The Deck Saigon</strong> (riverfront) | Farewell dinner at <strong>The Refinery</strong> (French‑Vietnamese) | — |<br />\n| 29  | HCMC – Departure | Private transfer to Tan Son Nhat International Airport | — | — | — |<br />\n| 30  | — | — | — | — | — |<br />\n<br />\n*Note: Days 27‑30 can be adjusted based on flight schedules or personal preferences.*<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>ACCOMMODATION</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n| City / Area | Property (verified) | Location | Facilities | Approx. nightly rate* |<br />\n|-------------|---------------------|----------|------------|-----------------------|<br />\n| Hanoi | Sofitel Legend Metropole Hanoi | Hoàn Kiếm District | Historic luxury, spa, rooftop bar, pool | US $250‑$350 |<br />\n| Ha Long Bay (cruise) | Paradise Luxury Cruise | On‑board | Private cabins, fine dining, kayaking, spa | US $300‑$450 per person (2‑night) |<br />\n| Sapa | Hotel de la Coupole – MGallery | Sapa town centre | Mountain views, heated pool, restaurant | US $120‑$180 |<br />\n| Hue | Azerai La Residence | Riverside, near Imperial City | Riverfront pool, spa, garden | US $180‑$260 |<br />\n| Hoi An | Anantara Hoi An Resort | Near Ancient Town, riverfront | Private beach, spa, cooking school | US $220‑$320 |<br />\n| Da Nang | InterContinental Danang Sun Peninsula Resort | Son Tra Peninsula | Private beach, 3‑restaurant complex, golf | US $350‑$500 |<br />\n| Nha Trang | Mia Resort Nha Trang | beachfront, near city | Infinity pool, spa, beachfront dining | US $180‑$250 |<br />\n| Đà Lạt | Ana Mandara Villas Dalat Resort &amp; Spa | Central Đà Lạt | Gardens, hot‑spring pool, spa | US $150‑$220 |<br />\n| Ho Chi Minh City | The Reverie Saigon | District 1, central | Opulent suites, rooftop pool, multiple restaurants | US $300‑$450 |<br />\n| Mekong Delta | Mekong Lodge (Boutique homestay) | My Tho | River view rooms, breakfast, bike rentals | US $80‑$120 |<br />\n| Phú Quốc | Fusion Resort Phú Quốc | Beachfront, An Thoi | All‑inclusive, multiple pools, water sports | US $250‑$350 |<br />\n<br />\n*Rates are <strong>estimates</strong> for high‑season (Feb‑May) and may vary with promotions, room type, and booking window. All properties are real and verified as of 2024.<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>FOOD AND EXPERIENCES</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Local cuisine highlights</strong> – Pho (Hanoi), Bún chả (Hanoi), Cao lầu (Hoi An), Bánh xèo (Đà Lạt), Gỏi cuốn (spring rolls, everywhere), Bún riêu (Nha Trang), Cơm tấm (Saigon), fresh seafood in Phú Quốc.  <br />\n- <strong>Dining recommendations</strong> –  <br />\n  - *Home* (Hanoi) – modern Vietnamese, reservation recommended.  <br />\n  - *Morning Glory* (Hoi An) – classic Hoi An dishes, popular with tourists.  <br />\n  - *La Maison 1888* (Da Nang) – French‑Vietnamese fine dining, Michelin‑starred chef.  <br />\n  - *Quince* (Ho Chi Minh City) – upscale tasting menu, requires advance booking.  <br />\n- <strong>Cultural experiences</strong> – Street‑food tours, lantern‑making workshop, traditional music performance in Hue, cooking class in Hoi An, homestay dinner with a Sapa', NULL, '2026-11-19 08:20:42'),
