(50, 'hetvi0796@gmail.com', 'ai', '<strong>TRIP OVERVIEW</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Destination:</strong> Tokyo, Japan  <br />\n- <strong>Duration:</strong> 5 days / 4 nights  <br />\n- <strong>Best travel period:</strong> Late March to early April (cherry‑blossom season) or October–November (pleasant autumn colors)  <br />\n- <strong>Estimated budget:</strong> ≈ USD 4,500 – 6,500 per person, depending on accommodation level and dining choices  <br />\n- <strong>Travel style:</strong> Luxury with optional budget‑friendly alternatives; blend of culture, modern design, gastronomy, and wellness  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DESTINATION HIGHLIGHTS</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Iconic attractions:</strong> Shibuya Crossing, Meiji Shrine, Senso‑ji Temple, Tokyo Skytree, Imperial Palace East Gardens  <br />\n- <strong>Landscapes &amp; landmarks:</strong> Tokyo Bay waterfront, Odaiba’s futuristic architecture, the gardens of Hamarikyu and Rikugien  <br />\n- <strong>Wellness experiences:</strong> Onsen‑style spa at <strong>Mandarin Oriental Tokyo</strong>, tea‑ceremony meditation at Hamarikyu Gardens, yoga studio “Yoga Tree” in Shibuya  <br />\n- <strong>Local activities:</strong> Sushi‑making workshop in Tsukiji, sumo‑practice viewing in Ryogoku, night‑time robot bar “Shinjuku Robot Restaurant”, shopping in Ginza and Harajuku  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DAY‑BY‑DAY ITINERARY</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 1 – Arrival &amp; Shibuya / Harajuku</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning:* Arrive at Narita/Haneda, private airport transfer (≈ USD 80–120) to hotel. Check‑in, settle.  <br />\n- *Afternoon:* Walk the Shibuya Crossing, visit Hachikō Statue, explore Shibuya Scramble Square observation deck (¥2,000).  <br />\n- *Evening:* Dinner at <strong>Uobei Shibuya Dogenzaka</strong> (conveyor‑belt sushi, ¥3,000–5,000 per person). Return to hotel; optional nightcap at the hotel’s rooftop bar.  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 2 – Cultural Core (Asakusa &amp; Ueno)</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning:* Guided tour of Senso‑ji Temple and Nakamise‑shopping street (private guide ≈ USD 150).  <br />\n- *Afternoon:* Visit Ueno Park, Tokyo National Museum (¥1,000) and Ameya‑Yokocho market for street snacks.  <br />\n- *Evening:* Kaiseki dinner at <strong>Kagurazaka Ishikawa</strong> (Michelin‑starred, ¥30,000–¥40,000 per person, reservation required).  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 3 – Modern Tokyo &amp; Bay Area</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning:* Tokyo Skytree (Tembo Deck ¥3,200) and Solamachi shopping.  <br />\n- *Afternoon:* Transfer to Odaiba via Yurikamome Line (¥650). Explore teamLab Borderless (¥3,200) and enjoy a waterfront stroll.  <br />\n- *Evening:* Sunset cruise on Tokyo Bay (≈ USD 120) followed by dinner at <strong>Sushi Sora</strong> (three‑Michelin‑star, ¥25,000–¥35,000).  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 4 – Imperial &amp; Wellness Day</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning:* Guided walk of the Imperial Palace East Gardens (free, reservation for palace tour optional).  <br />\n- *Afternoon:* Spa treatment at <strong>Mandarin Oriental Tokyo</strong> – “Signature Skyline Ritual” (≈ USD 250).  <br />\n- *Evening:* Explore Ginza’s upscale boutiques; dinner at <strong>Ginza Kojyu</strong> (kaiseki, ¥20,000–¥30,000).  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 5 – Departure</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning:* Optional sushi‑making class in Tsukiji (≈ USD 120) or a quick visit to the Tsukiji Outer Market for fresh seafood breakfast.  <br />\n- *Afternoon:* Check‑out, private transfer to airport (same rate as arrival).  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>ACCOMMODATION</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n| Hotel (Verified) | Location | Key Facilities | Approx. Nightly Rate* |<br />\n|------------------|----------|----------------|----------------------|<br />\n| <strong>Park Hyatt Tokyo</strong> | Shinjuku, near Shinjuku Station | 30‑m‑high rooms, New York Grill, spa, indoor pool, 24‑hr butler service | ¥70,000–¥100,000 (≈ USD 500–720) |<br />\n| <strong>Mandarin Oriental Tokyo</strong> | Nihonbashi, near Tokyo Station | Skyline spa, Michelin‑starred restaurant, rooftop bar, fitness center | ¥80,000–¥110,000 (≈ USD 570–790) |<br />\n| <strong>The Prince Gallery Tokyo Kioicho</strong> | Chiyoda, near Imperial Palace | Art‑focused design, rooftop pool, fine‑dining, private garden | ¥65,000–¥90,000 (≈ USD 460–640) |<br />\n| <strong>Hotel Ryumeikan Tokyo</strong> (budget‑friendly) | Near Tokyo Station | Classic Japanese décor, business lounge, easy rail access | ¥15,000–¥20,000 (≈ USD 110–140) |<br />\n<br />\n\\*Rates are indicative for March–April 2024, based on publicly listed prices; actual rates vary with booking window and room type.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>FOOD AND EXPERIENCES</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Local cuisine:</strong> Tempura at <strong>Tempura Kondo</strong> (Ginza, ¥8,000–¥12,000), ramen at <strong>Ichiran Shibuya</strong> (¥1,000–¥1,500), wagashi sweets in Asakusa.  <br />\n- <strong>Dining recommendations:</strong>  <br />\n  - <strong>Sukiyabashi Jiro</strong> (sushi, ¥30,000+ per person, reservation months ahead)  <br />\n  - <strong>Narisawa</strong> (innovative Japanese, ¥25,000–¥30,000)  <br />\n  - <strong>Ishikawa</strong> (kaiseki, ¥30,000–¥40,000) – for a special night.  <br />\n- <strong>Cultural experiences:</strong>  <br />\n  - Tea ceremony at <strong>Hamarikyu Gardens</strong> (¥3,000).  <br />\n  - Sumo stable visit in Ryogoku (guided tours ≈ USD 120).  <br />\n  - Nighttime robot bar show (≈ USD 80).  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>ESTIMATED BUDGET</strong> (per adult, mid‑range luxury)  <br />\n<br />\n| Category | Approx. Cost (USD) |<br />\n|----------|-------------------|<br />\n| Accommodation (4 nights) | 2,200 – 3,200 |<br />\n| Private airport transfers (round‑trip) | 200 – 250 |<br />\n| In‑city transport (subway, taxis, Yurikamome) | 120 – 180 |<br />\n| Meals (mix of high‑end and casual) | 1,200 – 1,800 |<br />\n| Activities &amp; entry fees (guides, museums, shows, spa) | 800 – 1,200 |<br />\n| Miscellaneous (tips, souvenirs, travel insurance) | 200 – 300 |<br />\n| <strong>Total Estimated Cost</strong> | <strong>4,720 – 6,930</strong> |<br />\n<br />\n*Assumptions:* travel in spring 2024, exchange rate ¥150 = USD 1, single traveler, taxes and service charges included where noted.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>IMPORTANT TRAVEL TIPS</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Weather &amp; clothing:</strong> Early April averages 12‑18 °C; bring a light jacket, layers, and comfortable walking shoes. Umbrella handy for occasional showers.  <br />\n- <strong>Transport:</strong> Purchase a prepaid <strong>Suica</strong> or <strong>Pasmo</strong> card for seamless subway and bus travel. For airport transfers, reputable limousine services (e.g., <strong>Tokyo Airport Limousine</strong>) are reliable.  <br />\n- <strong>Reservations:</strong> Michelin‑starred restaurants and popular experiences (sushi‑making, sumo viewing) require reservations 2–3 months in advance.  <br />\n- <strong>Safety:</strong> Tokyo is one of the safest major cities. Keep passport and cash in a secure travel wallet; credit cards widely accepted.  <br />\n- <strong>Documents:</strong> Visa‑free entry for many nationalities for stays up to 90 days; ensure passport validity of at least 6 months. Consider a <strong>Japan Rail Pass</strong> only if you plan day trips outside Tokyo (e.g., Nikko, Hakone).  <br />\n- <strong>Language:</strong> English signage is common in tourist areas, but a few Japanese phrases (e.g., “Arigatō” thank you) are appreciated.  <br />\n- <strong>Connectivity:</strong> Rent a pocket Wi‑Fi device (≈ USD 8 / day) or purchase a prepaid SIM at the airport.  <br />\n<br />\nEnjoy a seamless blend of tradition and cutting‑edge modernity on your five‑day Tokyo adventure!', NULL, '2026-11-19 15:09:16'),
(51, 'hetvi0796@gmail.com', 'user', 'Rajasthan trip for 10 days', NULL, '2026-11-19 15:09:43'),
(52, 'hetvi0796@gmail.com', 'ai', '<strong>TRIP OVERVIEW</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Destination:</strong> Rajasthan, India (Jaipur, Jodhpur, Jaisalmer, Udaipur, Pushkar)  <br />\n- <strong>Duration:</strong> 10 days / 9 nights  <br />\n- <strong>Best travel period:</strong> Late October – early March (cool, dry weather; peak of cultural festivals)  <br />\n- <strong>Estimated budget (luxury‑style, per person):</strong> US $3,500 – $5,000 (includes 5‑star accommodation, private transfers, guided tours, most meals, and entrance fees)  <br />\n- <strong>Travel style:</strong> Luxury cultural immersion with private transport, curated experiences, and wellness moments  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DESTINATION HIGHLIGHTS</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Jaipur (The Pink City)</strong> – Amber Fort, City Palace, Jantar Mantar, vibrant bazaars, Jaipur Literature Festival (January)  <br />\n- <strong>Jodhpur (The Blue City)</strong> – Mehrangarh Fort, Umaid Bhawan Palace, rooftop dining with sunset over the fort  <br />\n- <strong>Jaisalmer (The Golden City)</strong> – Jaisalmer Fort, Patwon Ki Haveli, camel safari in Sam Sand Dunes, star‑gazing night in a desert camp  <br />\n- <strong>Udaipur (City of Lakes)</strong> – Lake Pichola, City Palace, romantic boat ride, nearby Kumbhalgarh Fort for a day trek  <br />\n- <strong>Pushkar</strong> – Sacred lake, Brahma Temple, camel fair (if visiting in November)  <br />\n<br />\n*Wellness experiences* – Ayurvedic spa at The Oberoi Rajvilas (Udaipur), yoga session at a heritage haveli in Jodhpur, sunrise meditation on the dunes of Jaisalmer.  <br />\n<br />\n*Local activities* – Rajasthani cooking class, folk music &amp; dance show, pottery workshop in Jaipur, private guided market tours.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DAY‑BY‑DAY ITINERARY</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n| Day | Morning | Afternoon | Evening | Travel / Transfer |<br />\n|-----|---------|-----------|---------|-------------------|<br />\n| <strong>1</strong> | Arrive in Jaipur (Indira Gandhi Intl.). Private luxury SUV to hotel. | Check‑in at <strong>Rambagh Palace</strong>. Rest &amp; refresh. | Welcome dinner at <strong>Suvarna Mahal</strong> (Rambagh Palace). | Airport pickup (≈ 30 min). |<br />\n| <strong>2</strong> | Guided tour of Amber Fort (elephant ride optional). | Lunch at <strong>1135 AD</strong> (Amber Fort). Visit City Palace &amp; Jantar Mantar. | Sunset at Nahargarh Fort viewpoint. Dinner at <strong>Bar Palladio</strong>. | Private driver throughout day. |<br />\n| <strong>3</strong> | Early train/flight to Jodhpur (≈ 5 h by private car). | Check‑in at <strong>Umaid Bhawan Palace</strong>. Lunch at hotel. Visit Mehrangarh Fort and Jaswant Thada. | Rooftop dinner at <strong>Indique</strong> (Umaid Bhawan). | Private transfer, scenic stops en route. |<br />\n| <strong>4</strong> | Sunrise camel ride on the outskirts of Jodhpur. | Lunch at <strong>Jodhpur Café</strong> (heritage haveli). Explore the Clock Tower market. | Evening folk‑music show at <strong>Maharaja’s Palace</strong>. | Hotel concierge arranged camel ride. |<br />\n| <strong>5</strong> | Depart Jodhpur → Jaisalmer (≈ 5 h drive). | Check‑in at <strong>Suryagarh</strong> (luxury desert resort). Lunch at resort. Guided tour of Jaisalmer Fort &amp; Patwon Ki Haveli. | Sunset over the fort from <strong>Desert Camp</strong>. Dinner under the stars with Rajasthani thali. | Private SUV with air‑conditioned comfort. |<br />\n| <strong>6</strong> | Full‑day desert safari: camel trek, sandboarding, visit to <strong>Sam Sand Dunes</strong>. | Picnic lunch in the dunes. | Traditional Rajasthani cultural performance &amp; campfire dinner. | All transport included in desert camp package. |<br />\n| <strong>7</strong> | Morning flight/drive to Udaipur (≈ 6 h). | Check‑in at <strong>The Oberoi Rajvilas</strong>. Lunch by the lake. Visit City Palace &amp; Museum. | Boat cruise on Lake Pichola at sunset. Dinner at <strong>Upre</strong> (Lake Palace). | Private SUV; optional short flight from Jaisalmer to Udaipur (if preferred). |<br />\n| <strong>8</strong> | Yoga &amp; Ayurvedic spa session at the hotel. | Day‑trip to <strong>Kumbhalgarh Fort</strong> (UNESCO site) with guided trek. | Return to Udaipur. Dinner at <strong>Natraj Dining Hall</strong> (authentic Rajasthani thali). | Private guide &amp; driver for day trip. |<br />\n| <strong>9</strong> | Drive to Pushkar (≈ 3 h). | Check‑in at <strong>Ananta Spa &amp; Resorts</strong>. Explore Brahma Temple &amp; Pushkar Lake. | Sunset at <strong>Lake View Café</strong>. Dinner at <strong>The Sunset Café</strong>. | Private transfer; optional camel ride around the lake. |<br />\n| <strong>10</strong> | Leisure morning – optional hot‑air‑balloon ride over the desert (arranged in Jaipur) or spa. | Transfer to Jaipur airport (≈ 4 h). | Depart Rajasthan. | Private SUV to airport; flight onward. |<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>ACCOMMODATION</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n| City | Property (verified) | Location | Facilities | Approx. nightly rate* |<br />\n|------|---------------------|----------|------------|-----------------------|<br />\n| Jaipur | <strong>Rambagh Palace</strong> (Taj) | Near City Palace, Jaipur | Heritage palace, spa, pool, fine‑dining, private garden | US $550 – $800 |<br />\n| Jodhpur | <strong>Umaid Bhawan Palace</strong> (ITC) | Near Mehrangarh Fort | Luxury palace, golf course, spa, multiple restaurants | US $600 – $950 |<br />\n| Jaisalmer | <strong>Suryagarh</strong> | 6 km from Jaisalmer Fort | Desert resort, private pool, camel safari, spa | US $350 – $500 |<br />\n| Udaipur | <strong>The Oberoi Rajvilas</strong> | Lakeside, near City Palace | Lakeside villas, Ayurvedic spa, yoga pavilion, fine dining | US $500 – $750 |<br />\n| Pushkar | <strong>Ananta Spa &amp; Resorts</strong> | Lakeside, Pushkar | Spa, yoga decks, pool, vegetarian restaurant | US $180 – $250 |<br />\n<br />\n*Rates are indicative (based on 2024 pricing) and can vary with season and room category. Exact rates should be confirmed at booking.<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>FOOD AND EXPERIENCES</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Local cuisine highlights</strong> – Dal Baati Churma, Laal Maas (spicy mutton), Gatte Ki Sabzi, Ker Sangri, Rajasthani sweets (Mawa Kachori, Ghevar).  <br />\n- <strong>Dining recommendations</strong> –  <br />\n  - *Suvarna Mahal* (Rambagh Palace) – royal Rajasthani banquet.  <br />\n  - *Indique* (Umaid Bhawan) – rooftop views of Mehrangarh.  <br />\n  - *Upre* (Lake Palace, Udaipur) – lakeside fine dining.  <br />\n  - *Natraj Dining Hall* (Udaipur) – authentic thali at modest price.  <br />\n- <strong>Cultural experiences</strong> –  <br />\n  - Private Rajasthani cooking class in Jaipur (half‑day).  <br />\n  - Folk‑music &amp; dance show at <strong>Maharaja’s Palace</strong> (Jodhpur).  <br />\n  - Desert night camp with star‑gazing telescope in Jaisalmer.  <br />\n  - Optional hot‑air‑balloon ride over the Jaipur countryside (early morning).  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>ESTIMATED BUDGET</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n| Item | Approx. Cost (USD) per person |<br />\n|------|------------------------------|<br />\n| <strong>Accommodation</strong> (9 nights) | $5,200 – $7,200 |<br />\n| <strong>Private transport &amp; transfers</strong> | $800 – $1,200 |<br />\n| <strong>Domestic flights (if used)</strong> | $250 – $400 |<br />\n| <strong>Meals (incl. fine‑dining &amp; thalis)</strong> | $700 – $1,000 |<br />\n| <strong>Guided tours &amp; entry fees</strong> | $300 – $450 |<br />\n| <strong>Wellness &amp; activities (spa, yoga, desert camp)</strong> | $250 – $400 |<br />\n| <strong>Miscellaneous (tips, souvenirs, travel insurance)</strong> | $200 – $300 |<br />\n| <strong>Total estimated cost</strong> | <strong>$7,700 – $11,050</strong> |<br />\n*Assumptions: travel in double occupancy, mid‑range luxury rooms, private guide in each city, and standard seasonal rates. Prices are estimates; exact amounts will depend on travel dates and personal preferences.*<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>IMPORTANT TRAVEL TIPS</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Weather &amp; clothing:</strong> Daytime can be warm (20‑30 °C) even in winter; evenings are cool (5‑15 °C). Pack light layers, a warm sweater for desert nights, comfortable walking shoes, and a scarf for temple visits.  <br />\n- <strong>Transport:</strong> Private, air‑conditioned SUVs provide the most comfortable inter‑city travel. Domestic flights (Jaipur‑Jodhpur, Jodhpur‑Udaipur) can save time but are optional.  <br />\n- <strong>Reservations:</strong> Luxury hotels and popular experiences (e.g., desert camp, cooking class) book out 3‑4 months in advance, especially for the peak season (Oct‑Mar).  <br />\n- <strong>Safety:</strong> Rajasthan is generally safe for tourists. Keep valuables in hotel safes, use reputable transport providers, and stay hydrated.  <br />\n- <strong>Documents:</strong> Indian visa (e‑tourist visa) required for most nationalities; passport valid at least six months beyond travel dates. Carry a printed copy of your itinerary and hotel confirmations.  <br />\n- <strong>Health:</strong> No mandatory vaccinations, but routine vaccines should be up‑to‑date. Carry a basic medical kit; bottled water is recommended.  <br />\n- <strong>Cultural etiquette:</strong> Remove shoes before entering temples, dress modestly (shoulders and knees covered), and ask permission before photographing locals.  <br />\n<br />\nEnjoy a regal journey through Rajasthan’s palaces, deserts, and lakes—crafted for comfort, culture, and unforgettable memories.', NULL, '2026-11-19 15:09:49'),
(53, 'vmendapara432@rku.ac.in', 'ai', 'Tell me about the trip you\'re imagining — even if you only have a destination, a mood, or a season in mind.', NULL, '2026-11-20 03:42:29'),
(54, 'vmendapara432@rku.ac.in', 'user', 'Plan me a 5-day winter trip to Switzerland', NULL, '2026-11-20 03:42:35');
INSERT INTO `ai_chats` (`id`, `user_email`, `sender`, `message`, `image_url`, `created_at`) VALUES
(55, 'vmendapara432@rku.ac.in', 'ai', '<strong>TRIP OVERVIEW</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Destination:</strong> Switzerland (Western Alps)  <br />\n- <strong>Duration:</strong> 5 days (Winter)  <br />\n- <strong>Best travel period:</strong> Mid‑December to early March – optimal for snow, festive markets and reliable ski conditions.  <br />\n- <strong>Estimated budget (per person):</strong> CHF 3,200 – CHF 4,800 (≈ USD 3,500 – 5,300) – includes mid‑range luxury accommodation, transport, meals and activities; exact cost will vary with hotel category and ski‑pass choices.  <br />\n- <strong>Travel style:</strong> Luxury‑comfort with a blend of cultural sightseeing, winter sports and wellness experiences.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DESTINATION HIGHLIGHTS</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Zermatt &amp; the Matterhorn:</strong> Iconic snow‑capped peak, world‑class ski area, Glacier Paradise (Europe’s highest cable car station).  <br />\n- <strong>Jungfraujoch – “Top of Europe”:</strong> Spectacular Alpine views, Ice Palace, Sphinx Observatory.  <br />\n- <strong>Lucerne:</strong> Charming medieval old town, Chapel Bridge, lakeside promenade, nearby Mt. Pilatus (winter cogwheel railway).  <br />\n- <strong>Interlaken:</strong> Gateway to the Bernese Oberland, winter hiking, and luxury spa resorts.  <br />\n- <strong>St. Moritz:</strong> Legendary winter resort, frozen lake for skating, world‑renowned gourmet restaurants.  <br />\n<br />\nWellness options include hotel spas (thermal pools, sauna circuits, Alpine‑herb treatments) and mountain‑air yoga sessions.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DAY‑BY‑DAY ITINERARY</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 1 – Arrival in Zurich → Lucerne</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning:* Fly into Zurich Airport, private transfer (≈ 45 min) to Lucerne.  <br />\n- *Afternoon:* Check‑in at <strong>Hotel des Balances</strong> (historic 4‑star boutique, lake‑front). Stroll the Old Town, visit the Chapel Bridge and the Lion Monument.  <br />\n- *Evening:* Dinner at <strong>Restaurant Focus</strong> (Michelin‑starred, modern Swiss cuisine).  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 2 – Lucerne &amp; Mt. Pilatus</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning:* Cogwheel railway to Mt. Pilatus (winter schedule). Snow‑shoe walk on the “Dragon Trail”.  <br />\n- *Afternoon:* Return to Lucerne; optional lake cruise on Lake Lucerne (heated cabin).  <br />\n- *Evening:* Relax in the hotel spa; enjoy a fondue dinner at <strong>Wirtshaus Galliker</strong> (traditional).  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 3 – Travel to Zermatt – Matterhorn Experience</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning:* Swiss Federal Railways (SBB) Glacier Express (first‑class) Zurich → Zermatt (≈ 3.5 h). Scenic winter panorama.  <br />\n- *Afternoon:* Check‑in at <strong>Hotel Monte Rosa</strong> (historic 4‑star, central location). Take the Matterhorn Glacier Paradise cable car to the summit; explore the Ice Palace.  <br />\n- *Evening:* Gourmet dinner at <strong>Restaurant Whymper-Stube</strong> (fondue &amp; raclette).  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 4 – Ski &amp; Wellness in Zermatt</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning:* Full‑day ski pass (Zermatt‑Cervinia area). Private ski instructor optional.  <br />\n- *Afternoon:* Après‑ski at <strong>The Omnia</strong> lounge (luxury hotel, panoramic views).  <br />\n- *Evening:* Spa treatment at <strong>The Omnia</strong> (thermal pool, Alpine stone massage). Light dinner at the hotel’s <strong>Restaurant Omnia</strong>.  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 5 – Jungfraujoch &amp; Departure via Interlaken</strong>  <br />\n- *Early morning:* Transfer by train to Interlaken Ost, then to Jungfraujoch (≈ 2 h). Visit Ice Palace, Sphinx Observatory, and enjoy a hot chocolate on the “Top of Europe”.  <br />\n- *Afternoon:* Return to Interlaken; quick lunch at <strong>Husi Bierhaus</strong> (Swiss‑style tavern). Private transfer to Zurich Airport (≈ 2 h) for departure.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>ACCOMMODATION</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n| City / Area | Property (verified) | Location | Facilities | Approx. nightly rate* |<br />\n|-------------|---------------------|----------|------------|-----------------------|<br />\n| Lucerne | Hotel des Balances (4★) | Near Lake &amp; Old Town | Lake view rooms, rooftop terrace, restaurant, spa | CHF 250‑300 |<br />\n| Zermatt | Hotel Monte Rosa (4★) | Central, car‑free village | Alpine décor, restaurant, wellness area | CHF 220‑280 |<br />\n| Zermatt (optional upgrade) | The Omnia (5★) | Cliffside, 5‑min walk from lifts | Infinity pool, spa, fine‑dining, private ski storage | CHF 380‑460 |<br />\n<br />\n*Rates are indicative for December‑February, based on publicly listed prices; actual rates depend on exact dates and availability.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>FOOD AND EXPERIENCES</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Local cuisine:</strong> Swiss cheese fondue, raclette, rösti, Zürcher Geschnetzeltes, fresh Alpine trout.  <br />\n- <strong>Dining highlights:</strong>  <br />\n  - *Restaurant Focus* (Lucerne) – contemporary tasting menu, Michelin‑starred.  <br />\n  - *Whymper‑Stube* (Zermatt) – classic Alpine fondue in a historic chalet.  <br />\n  - *The Omnia Restaurant* – seasonal Swiss‑Mediterranean fusion with panoramic mountain views.  <br />\n- <strong>Cultural experiences:</strong>  <br />\n  - Lucerne’s Christmas market (if traveling early December).  <br />\n  - Evening “Swiss Night” concert at the Lucerne Culture and Congress Centre (KCL).  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>ESTIMATED BUDGET</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n| Category | Approx. Cost (CHF) | Notes |<br />\n|----------|-------------------|-------|<br />\n| Accommodation (4 nights) | 1,100 – 1,800 | Based on mid‑range luxury hotels; upgrade to 5★ adds ~CHF 500. |<br />\n| Transport | 350 – 450 | Swiss Travel Pass (3‑day) + Glacier Express first‑class + airport transfers. |<br />\n| Ski &amp; mountain passes | 250 – 350 | Zermatt ski pass (2 days) + Jungfraujoch ticket. |<br />\n| Food &amp; dining | 500 – 750 | Mix of fine‑dining (≈ CHF 120 per dinner) and casual meals. |<br />\n| Activities &amp; entry fees | 150 – 200 | Pilatus cogwheel, Ice Palace, spa treatments (optional). |<br />\n| Miscellaneous (tips, souvenirs) | 150 – 200 |  |<br />\n| <strong>Total estimated</strong> | <strong>2,500 – 3,750</strong> | Per person; assumes shared private transfers. |<br />\n<br />\n*All figures are estimates; exact amounts will vary with hotel choice, travel dates and personal spending preferences.*<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>IMPORTANT TRAVEL TIPS</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Weather &amp; clothing:</strong> Expect temperatures between –5 °C and 5 °C in the valleys, colder at high altitudes. Pack insulated winter coat, waterproof ski pants, thermal layers, gloves, hat, and sturdy insulated boots.  <br />\n- <strong>Transport:</strong> The Swiss Travel Pass offers unlimited travel on most trains, buses and boats; it also provides discounts on many mountain railways. Reserve Glacier Express seats in advance (mandatory).  <br />\n- <strong>Reservations:</strong> Book hotels and ski passes at least 2–3 months ahead for winter season. Fine‑dining restaurants often require reservations 2 weeks prior.  <br />\n- <strong>Safety:</strong> Alpine weather can change rapidly; always check local forecasts before heading to high‑altitude sites. Carry a basic first‑aid kit and stay on marked trails.  <br />\n- <strong>Documents:</strong> A valid passport is required; EU/EEA citizens can enter with a national ID. Non‑EU travelers need a Schengen visa if required. Carry travel insurance covering winter sports.  <br />\n- <strong>Currency:</strong> Swiss Franc (CHF). Credit cards are widely accepted, but keep some cash for small mountain‑village shops.  <br />\n- <strong>Language:</strong> German, French, Italian and Romansh are official languages; English is commonly spoken in tourist areas.  <br />\n<br />\nEnjoy a seamless blend of Alpine adventure, festive charm and luxurious relaxation on your Swiss winter getaway!', NULL, '2026-11-20 03:42:40'),
(56, 'vmendapara432@rku.ac.in', 'user', 'Plan me a luxury trip to Coorg', NULL, '2026-11-20 04:03:18'),
(57, 'vmendapara432@rku.ac.in', 'ai', '<strong>TRIP OVERVIEW</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Destination:</strong> Coorg (Kodagu), Karnataka, India  <br />\n- <strong>Duration:</strong> 5 nights / 6 days  <br />\n- <strong>Best travel period:</strong> October – March (cool, dry weather; coffee harvest season adds cultural interest)  <br />\n- <strong>Estimated budget:</strong> ≈ ₹ 3,00,000 – ₹ 4,20,000 for two adults (luxury accommodation, private transfers, fine dining, guided activities)  <br />\n- <strong>Travel style:</strong> Luxury with emphasis on privacy, wellness, and curated experiences  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DESTINATION HIGHLIGHTS</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Natural attractions:</strong> Abbey Falls, Iruppu Falls, Talacauvery (source of the Cauvery River), Raja’s Seat sunset viewpoint, coffee &amp; spice plantations, mist‑covered hills of the Western Ghats.  <br />\n- <strong>Wildlife &amp; adventure:</strong> Nagarhole National Park (safari), Dubare Elephant Camp (elephant interaction).  <br />\n- <strong>Wellness experiences:</strong> Ayurvedic spa treatments, yoga sessions, plantation‑themed wellness rituals offered by premium resorts.  <br />\n- <strong>Cultural touches:</strong> Traditional Kodava cuisine, folk dance performances, visits to historic Madikeri Fort and local markets.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DAY‑BY‑DAY ITINERARY</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 1 – Arrival &amp; Relaxation</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning:* Fly into Bangalore (BLR). Private, air‑conditioned sedan picks you up (≈ 6 h drive).  <br />\n- *Afternoon:* Check‑in at <strong>Taj Madikeri Resort &amp; Spa</strong> (Madikeri). Welcome drink and brief orientation.  <br />\n- *Evening:* Sunset walk on the resort’s private garden terrace, followed by a gourmet dinner featuring Coorgi specialties (e.g., pandi curry, bamboo shoot).  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 2 – Coffee Plantation &amp; Cultural Immersion</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning:* Private guided tour of a certified organic coffee plantation (e.g., <strong>Coffee Board’s Plantation at Kushalnagar</strong>). Hands‑on coffee‑bean picking and tasting session.  <br />\n- *Afternoon:* Lunch at the plantation’s farm‑to‑table restaurant (menu curated with local produce). Return to resort for a spa treatment (Ayurvedic Abhyanga).  <br />\n- *Evening:* Attend a Kodava folk‑dance performance arranged by the resort.  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 3 – Scenic Exploration &amp; Wellness</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning:* Transfer to <strong>The Tamara Coorg</strong> (near Kushalnagar). Check‑in and enjoy a sunrise yoga class overlooking the hills.  <br />\n- *Afternoon:* Guided hike to <strong>Abbey Falls</strong> and <strong>Raja’s Seat</strong> with a private naturalist. Picnic lunch with local cheese and honey.  <br />\n- *Evening:* Return to The Tamara for a riverside dinner; optional night‑time stargazing session with a local astronomer.  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 4 – Wildlife Safari &amp; Elephant Experience</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning:* Early‑morning private safari in <strong>Nagarhole National Park</strong> (jeep with a naturalist guide). Spot tigers, elephants, and a variety of birdlife.  <br />\n- *Afternoon:* Lunch at the park’s eco‑lodge (pre‑booked). Transfer to <strong>Dubare Elephant Camp</strong> for a guided elephant‑bath and feeding experience (guided by trained mahouts).  <br />\n- *Evening:* Return to The Tamara. Relax in the infinity pool; dinner featuring a multi‑course tasting menu paired with regional wines.  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 5 – Leisure &amp; Personalized Activities</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning:* Optional cooking class at the resort (learn to prepare traditional Coorgi dishes).  <br />\n- *Afternoon:* Free time for spa, golf at the resort’s 9‑hole course, or a private boat ride on the nearby <strong>Kaveri River</strong>.  <br />\n- *Evening:* Farewell dinner on a private terrace with a curated music ensemble playing local instruments.  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 6 – Departure</strong>  <br />\n- *Morning:* Leisurely breakfast; checkout.  <br />\n- *Transfer:* Private sedan to Bangalore Airport (or Mysore Airport if preferred).  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>ACCOMMODATION</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n| Property (Verified) | Location | Key Facilities | Approx. Nightly Rate* |<br />\n|---------------------|----------|----------------|----------------------|<br />\n| Taj Madikeri Resort &amp; Spa | Madikeri | 5‑star, spa, infinity pool, multiple dining venues, private garden, airport transfer service | ₹ 22,000 – ₹ 30,000 (standard rooms) |<br />\n| The Tamara Coorg | Near Kushalnagar | 5‑star boutique, river‑front villas, yoga pavilion, Ayurvedic spa, organic restaurant, golf course | ₹ 18,000 – ₹ 25,000 (villa) |<br />\n| Evolve Back, Coorg (formerly Orange County) | Madikeri outskirts | Luxury villas, coffee‑plantation views, heritage décor, spa, private pool, guided plantation tours | ₹ 20,000 – ₹ 28,000 (villa) |<br />\n<br />\n\\*Rates are indicative for the high‑season (Oct‑Mar) and reflect publicly listed prices on the hotels’ official websites as of 2024. Exact rates depend on room type, view, and booking window.<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>FOOD AND EXPERIENCES</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Local cuisine highlights:</strong> Pandi Curry (pork), Kadumbuttu (rice dumplings), Nool Puttu (rice noodles), Bamboo Shoot Fry, Coorgi honey, fresh coffee.  <br />\n- <strong>Dining recommendations:</strong>  <br />\n  - *The Spice Route* at Taj Madikeri – fine‑dining with a focus on regional ingredients.  <br />\n  - *The Tamara’s Riverside Grill* – grilled specialties with a view of the Kaveri.  <br />\n  - *Coorg Cuisine* at Evolve Back – traditional Kodava dishes served in a heritage setting.  <br />\n- <strong>Cultural experiences:</strong> Private Kodava dance (Uppatt) show, guided visits to Madikeri market for spice shopping, coffee‑brew masterclass.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>ESTIMATED BUDGET</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n| Category | Approx. Cost (INR) | Notes |<br />\n|----------|-------------------|-------|<br />\n| Accommodation (5 nights) | ₹ 1,00,000 – ₹ 1,40,000 | Based on mid‑range of rates above, double occupancy |<br />\n| Private ground transport (airport‑hotel‑safari‑excursions) | ₹ 80,000 – ₹ 1,00,000 | Includes driver, fuel, insurance |<br />\n| Food &amp; beverages (incl. fine‑dining, private meals) | ₹ 80,000 – ₹ 1,00,000 | 3‑4 meals per day, wine pairings, special experiences |<br />\n| Activities &amp; entry fees (safari, plantation tours, spa) | ₹ 60,000 – ₹ 80,000 | Guided tours, spa packages, elephant camp |<br />\n| Miscellaneous (tips, taxes, travel insurance) | ₹ 30,000 – ₹ 40,000 | 10 % contingency |<br />\n| <strong>Total estimated cost</strong> | <strong>₹ 3,50,000 – ₹ 4,20,000</strong> | For two adults; assumes luxury tier |<br />\n<br />\n*All figures are estimates based on publicly available rates (2024) and may vary with exact travel dates and availability.*<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>IMPORTANT TRAVEL TIPS</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Weather &amp; clothing:</strong> Daytime 15‑25 °C; evenings can drop to 8‑12 °C. Pack layered clothing, a light down jacket, comfortable walking shoes, and rain gear (occasional showers).  <br />\n- <strong>Transport:</strong> Private sedan is the most comfortable option; road conditions are good but winding. Consider a driver familiar with hill driving.  <br />\n- <strong>Reservations:</strong> Luxury resorts fill quickly during peak season; book at least 3 months in advance. Safari permits for Nagarhole should be secured through the resort’s concierge.  <br />\n- <strong>Safety:</strong> Coorg is generally safe for tourists. Keep valuables in hotel safe. Follow guide instructions during wildlife encounters.  <br />\n- <strong>Documents:</strong> Valid passport, Indian visa (if required), travel insurance covering medical evacuation, and a copy of COVID‑19 vaccination proof (if still mandated).  <br />\n- <strong>Health:</strong> Altitude is modest, but stay hydrated. Carry any personal medication; basic medical facilities are available in Madikeri, but major hospitals are in Mysore/Bangalore.  <br />\n<br />\nEnjoy a refined, nature‑immersed escape in the “Scotland of India,” where luxury blends seamlessly with the verdant hills and fragrant coffee estates of Coorg.', NULL, '2026-11-20 04:03:23'),
