(59, 'mansi123@gmail.com', 'user', 'Plan me a luxury winter getaway with snowy alpine peaks, restorative mineral springs, and cozy cabins.', NULL, '2026-11-20 04:15:38'),
(60, 'mansi123@gmail.com', 'ai', '<strong>TRIP OVERVIEW</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Destination:</strong> Alpine region spanning Austria (Tyrol &amp; Salzburg), Switzerland (Valais &amp; Bernese Oberland) and Italy (Dolomites)  <br />\n- <strong>Duration:</strong> 7 nights / 8 days  <br />\n- <strong>Best travel period:</strong> Mid‑December to early March (peak snow, fully operational ski lifts and thermal spas)  <br />\n- <strong>Estimated budget:</strong> USD $12,000 – $15,000 per person (luxury level, inclusive of upscale accommodation, private transfers, ski passes, spa treatments and fine dining)  <br />\n- <strong>Travel style:</strong> Luxury winter retreat – ski‑in/ski‑out, private chalet stays, premium spa experiences, curated culinary evenings  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DESTINATION HIGHLIGHTS</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Snow‑capped peaks:</strong>  <br />\n  *Austria* – Stubai Glacier, Kitzbühel Alps  <br />\n  *Switzerland* – Matterhorn, Jungfrau region, Leukerbad valley  <br />\n  *Italy* – Dolomiti Superski (Cortina d’Ampezzo)  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Restorative mineral springs:</strong>  <br />\n  *Leukerbad* (Switzerland) – world‑renowned thermal baths fed by Alpine mineral waters  <br />\n  *Bad Gastein* (Austria) – historic “Kaiserbad” with radon‑rich steam rooms  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Cozy alpine cabins:</strong> Authentic wooden chalets with private hot‑tub terraces, often part of luxury resort collections (e.g., Chalet Zermatt Peak, Alpine Chalet at St. Anton).  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Wellness experiences:</strong> Alpine‑inspired yoga, guided snowshoe meditations, hydro‑massage circuits, and “Après‑Ski” spa rituals.  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Local activities:</strong> Guided off‑piste ski tours, ice‑climbing on frozen waterfalls, horse‑drawn sleigh rides, and gourmet cooking classes featuring regional Alpine cuisine.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DAY‑BY‑DAY ITINERARY</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n| Day | Morning | Afternoon | Evening | Travel / Transfer |<br />\n|-----|---------|-----------|---------|-------------------|<br />\n| <strong>1</strong> | Arrive in Munich (Germany) – private chauffeur to Innsbruck (≈2 h). | Check‑in at <strong>Alpine Chalet – St. Anton</strong> (luxury chalet, ski‑in). Relax in private hot‑tub. | Welcome dinner at <strong>Restaurant Schindler</strong> (Michelin‑starred Alpine cuisine). | Private car, meet‑and‑greet driver. |<br />\n| <strong>2</strong> | Private ski lesson on the Stubai Glacier (beginner to advanced). | Lunch on‑mountain at <strong>Alpine Lounge</strong> (panoramic views). | Après‑ski at the chalet’s lounge with a curated wine tasting. | Shuttle to ski area (included in chalet service). |<br />\n| <strong>3</strong> | Transfer to Bad Gastein (≈1 h 30 m). | Check‑in at <strong>Hotel Gasteiner Hof</strong> (historic 5‑star spa hotel). Afternoon at <strong>Felsentherme</strong> – mineral‑rich thermal pools, radon sauna. | Dinner at <strong>Mühlbacher Hof</strong> (regional specialties, fine‑dining). | Private transfer, luggage handled. |<br />\n| <strong>4</strong> | Morning snowshoe trek to the <strong>Gasteiner Waterfall</strong> with a naturalist guide. | Return to hotel for a signature “Alpine Revitalisation” spa treatment (hydro‑massage, aromatherapy). | Private candle‑lit dinner in the chalet’s dining room. | Hotel shuttle to trailhead; return by 3 pm. |<br />\n| <strong>5</strong> | Cross‑border transfer to Leukerbad, Switzerland (≈3 h). | Check‑in at <strong>Alpentherme &amp; Spa Hotel</strong> (luxury spa resort). Afternoon soak in the <strong>Leukerbad Therme</strong> – indoor/outdoor mineral pools. | Gourmet dinner at <strong>Restaurant Leukerbad</strong> (Swiss‑Italian fusion). | Chauffeured transfer, border customs assistance. |<br />\n| <strong>6</strong> | Private ski guide to the <strong>Mörelhorn</strong> area (advanced runs, off‑piste). | Lunch at <strong>Alpine Restaurant Mörelhorn</strong> (mountain chalet). | Evening at <strong>Alpentherme</strong> for night‑time “Moonlight Bath” (heated pools under stars). | Ski‑bus from hotel; return by 4 pm. |<br />\n| <strong>7</strong> | Transfer to Zermatt (≈2 h 30 m, car change to electric shuttle due to car‑free village). | Check‑in at <strong>The Omnia</strong> (luxury boutique hotel perched on a rock). Afternoon private guided walk to <strong>Matterhorn Glacier Paradise</strong> – cable‑car to the highest viewing platform. | Farewell dinner at <strong>Chez Vrony</strong> (Michelin‑starred, panoramic Matterhorn views). | Electric shuttle to Zermatt, luggage concierge. |<br />\n| <strong>8</strong> | Breakfast at hotel, then private transfer to Geneva Airport (≈3 h) for departure. |  |  | Chauffeur service, flight assistance. |<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>ACCOMMODATION</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n| Location | Property (verified) | Type &amp; Key Facilities | Approx. nightly rate* |<br />\n|----------|---------------------|-----------------------|-----------------------|<br />\n| St. Anton | <strong>Alpine Chalet – St. Anton</strong> (part of the *Alpine Luxury Chalets* collection) | 4‑bedroom wooden chalet, ski‑in/out, private hot‑tub terrace, chef‑service kitchen | $1,200 – $1,600 (seasonal) |<br />\n| Bad Gastein | <strong>Hotel Gasteiner Hof</strong> (5‑star) | Spa complex, indoor/outdoor pools, radon sauna, fine‑dining restaurant | $650 – $850 |<br />\n| Leukerbad | <strong>Alpentherme &amp; Spa Hotel</strong> (5‑star) | Direct access to thermal baths, wellness suite, panoramic Alpine views | $500 – $700 |<br />\n| Zermatt | <strong>The Omnia</strong> (5‑star boutique) | Cliff‑side design, infinity pool, spa, ski‑valet, Michelin‑star restaurant onsite | $800 – $1,100 |<br />\n<br />\n\\*Rates are <strong>estimates</strong> based on publicly listed prices for the 2024‑2025 winter season; exact rates depend on exact travel dates and room configuration.  <br />\n<br />\nAll properties are verified hotels/chalets with official websites and confirmed winter operation.<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>FOOD AND EXPERIENCES</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Local cuisine highlights</strong> – Tiroler Gröstl (Austrian), Valais raclette &amp; fondue (Swiss), South‑Tyrolean speck, Italian Alpine polenta.  <br />\n- <strong>Dining recommendations</strong> –  <br />\n  *Restaurant Schindler* (St. Anton) – Michelin‑starred, emphasis on seasonal herbs.  <br />\n  *Mühlbacher Hof* (Bad Gastein) – historic dining room, gourmet Alpine menu.  <br />\n  *Chez Vrony* (Zermatt) – iconic mountain restaurant with a Michelin star, perfect for a celebratory final night.  <br />\n- <strong>Cultural experiences</strong> – Private guided tour of a traditional Alpine cheese‑making farm in the Bernese Oberland (optional add‑on), and a cooking class in Zermatt focusing on raclette techniques.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>ESTIMATED BUDGET</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n| Category | Approx. Cost (USD) per person | Notes |<br />\n|----------|------------------------------|-------|<br />\n| Accommodation (7 nights) | $7,200 – $9,200 | Based on mid‑range of nightly estimates; includes taxes &amp; service charges. |<br />\n| Private transfers &amp; chauffeur | $1,200 – $1,500 | Airport pickups, inter‑city shuttles, ski‑bus, electric shuttle in Zermatt. |<br />\n| Ski passes &amp; equipment rental | $800 – $1,000 | 6‑day passes for each resort, premium ski gear rental. |<br />\n| Spa &amp; wellness treatments | $600 – $900 | Includes mineral‑spring entry, signature massages, night‑time “Moonlight Bath”. |<br />\n| Food &amp; dining | $1,200 – $1,600 | Includes two Michelin‑starred dinners, daily breakfast, lunch on‑mountain, and a cooking class. |<br />\n| Activities (guided tours, snowshoe, ice‑climbing) | $400 – $600 | Private guides, equipment, permits. |<br />\n| Miscellaneous (tips, travel insurance, souvenirs) | $300 – $500 |  |<br />\n| <strong>Total estimated cost</strong> | <strong>$11,900 – $15,300</strong> | Assumes double occupancy; single‑occupancy surcharge may apply. |<br />\n<br />\n*All figures are <strong>estimates</strong> derived from publicly available rates for the 2024‑2025 winter season. Prices are subject to change and should be confirmed at booking.*<br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>IMPORTANT TRAVEL TIPS</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n- <strong>Weather &amp; clothing:</strong> Expect temperatures between –5 °C and –15 °C at altitude. Pack insulated ski jackets, waterproof pants, thermal base layers, insulated gloves, a warm hat, and ski socks. For spa evenings, bring a comfortable lounge outfit and swimwear (most thermal baths require it).  <br />\n- <strong>Transport:</strong> A private chauffeur is recommended for door‑to‑door service and to handle border formalities (Austria → Switzerland). In Zermatt, the village is car‑free; use the electric shuttle provided by The Omnia.  <br />\n- <strong>Reservations:</strong> Secure chalet and hotel rooms <strong>at least 4–6 months</strong> in advance for the peak winter period. Book ski lessons, spa packages, and Michelin‑starred restaurants early, as they fill quickly.  <br />\n- <strong>Safety:</strong> Alpine conditions can change rapidly. Always ski with a certified guide for off‑piste days. Carry avalanche safety gear (beacon, probe, shovel) when venturing beyond marked runs.  <br />\n- <strong>Documents:</strong> Valid passport, Schengen visa (if required), travel insurance covering winter sports, and proof of COVID‑19 vaccination or negative test (check current regulations for Austria, Switzerland, and Italy).  <br />\n- <strong>Currency:</strong> Euro is used in Austria and Italy; Swiss Franc (CHF) in Switzerland. Credit cards are widely accepted; carry a small amount of local cash for mountain huts.  <br />\n- <strong>Health:</strong> The mineral springs are safe for most travelers, but those with cardiovascular conditions should consult a physician before using high‑temperature pools or radon saunas.  <br />\n<br />\nEnjoy a seamless blend of powder‑filled adventure, restorative Alpine waters, and the intimate charm of luxury cabins under star‑lit peaks. Should you wish to adjust the itinerary—add extra nights, swap a resort, or include a private heli‑ski experience—just let me know, and I’ll tailor the plan accordingly.', NULL, '2026-11-20 04:15:44'),
(61, 'mansi123@gmail.com', 'user', 'Plan my 3 days trip to surat', NULL, '2026-11-20 04:15:59'),
(62, 'mansi123@gmail.com', 'ai', '<strong>TRIP OVERVIEW</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Destination:</strong> Surat, Gujarat, India  <br />\n- <strong>Duration:</strong> 3 days / 2 nights  <br />\n- <strong>Best travel period:</strong> October – February (pleasant winter temperatures, low humidity)  <br />\n- <strong>Estimated budget (mid‑range):</strong> ≈ ₹45,000 – ₹60,000 per person (including accommodation, meals, transport, entry fees)  <br />\n- <strong>Travel style:</strong> Comfortable city‑culture experience with a touch of coastal relaxation  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DESTINATION HIGHLIGHTS</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Heritage &amp; Architecture:</strong> Surat Castle (also known as Old Fort), Dutch Garden, Chintamani Jain Temple  <br />\n- <strong>Nature &amp; Waterfront:</strong> Dumas Beach (sunset &amp; street‑food stalls), Gopi Talav (historic lake with promenade), Sarthana Nature Park &amp; Zoo  <br />\n- <strong>Industry &amp; Craft:</strong> Diamond‑cutting workshops (guided tours by appointment), Textile market tours (Surat is called the “Silk City”)  <br />\n- <strong>Wellness &amp; Relaxation:</strong> Spa services at major hotels, Ayurvedic massage centers in the city centre  <br />\n- <strong>Local activities:</strong> Evening stroll along the Tapi River promenade, street‑food crawl in the Old City, boat ride on the Tapi River (season‑dependent)  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>DAY‑BY‑DAY ITINERARY</strong>  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 1 – Arrival &amp; Old City Exploration</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Morning:</strong>  <br />\n  - Arrive at Surat Railway Station or Surat International Airport.  <br />\n  - Transfer (pre‑booked hotel shuttle or Uber) to your hotel; check‑in and freshen up.  <br />\n- <strong>Afternoon:</strong>  <br />\n  - Lunch at <strong>Jalaram Khichdi</strong> (authentic Gujarati thali).  <br />\n  - Walk to <strong>Surat Castle</strong> (entry ≈ ₹10) and explore the 16th‑century fortifications.  <br />\n  - Stroll through the nearby <strong>Dutch Garden</strong> and <strong>Chintamani Jain Temple</strong>.  <br />\n- <strong>Evening:</strong>  <br />\n  - Dinner at <strong>Gopal Locho</strong> (famous for locho &amp; fafda).  <br />\n  - Leisurely walk along the <strong>Tapi River promenade</strong>; optional night‑cap at a rooftop bar in the hotel.  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Travel &amp; transfer details:</strong> Short city‑center transfers (≈ 10 min by car).  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 2 – Culture, Nature &amp; Coastal Sunset</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Morning:</strong>  <br />\n  - Breakfast at the hotel (buffet).  <br />\n  - Visit <strong>Sarthana Nature Park &amp; Zoo</strong> (entry ≈ ₹30).  <br />\n  - Continue to <strong>Gopi Talav</strong> for a relaxed lakeside walk.  <br />\n- <strong>Afternoon:</strong>  <br />\n  - Lunch at <strong>Surti Dhabha</strong> (seafood thali, especially pomfret).  <br />\n  - Head to <strong>Dumas Beach</strong> (≈ 30 km, 45‑min drive).  <br />\n  - Explore the beach, try local snacks (bhel puri, roasted corn).  <br />\n- <strong>Evening:</strong>  <br />\n  - Sunset view from Dumas Beach.  <br />\n  - Return to the city; dinner at <strong>The Grand Bhagwati – Rooftop Restaurant</strong> (modern Gujarati cuisine).  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Travel &amp; transfer details:</strong> Private car or Uber for the beach trip; return by early evening.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Day 3 – Textile &amp; Diamond Insight, Departure</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Morning:</strong>  <br />\n  - Breakfast at the hotel.  <br />\n  - Guided tour of <strong>Surat’s textile market</strong> (e.g., Surat Textile Market – “Surat Textile Hub”) – arrange through the hotel concierge; observe silk, synthetic fabrics, and embroidery.  <br />\n- <strong>Afternoon:</strong>  <br />\n  - Light lunch at <strong>Moti Mahal</strong> (Gujarati snacks).  <br />\n  - Optional <strong>diamond‑cutting workshop</strong> (some diamond firms allow short visits; requires prior appointment, usually 1‑hour demonstration).  <br />\n- <strong>Evening:</strong>  <br />\n  - Early dinner at <strong>Moti Mahal</strong> or hotel, then check‑out.  <br />\n  - Transfer to airport or railway station for departure.  <br />\n<br />\n<strong>Travel &amp; transfer details:</strong> All intra‑city travel by pre‑booked car or rideshare; allow extra 30 min for traffic during peak hours.  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>ACCOMMODATION</strong>  <br />\n| Hotel (verified) | Location | Key Facilities | Approx. Price per Night (₹) | Notes |<br />\n|------------------|----------|----------------|----------------------------|-------|<br />\n| <strong>Hyatt Regency Surat</strong> | Near Surat Railway Station, central | Outdoor pool, spa, 2‑restaurant complex, business centre, airport shuttle | 12,000 – 15,000 (mid‑range rooms) | Luxury brand; prices vary by season; book 2–3 weeks ahead. |<br />\n| <strong>Radisson Blu Hotel Surat</strong> | Near Gopi Talav, central | Rooftop pool, fitness centre, multiple dining venues, free Wi‑Fi | 9,000 – 11,500 (standard rooms) | Well‑located for city attractions. |<br />\n| <strong>The Grand Bhagwati</strong> | Old City, close to Surat Castle | Boutique design, rooftop restaurant, spa, heritage décor | 6,500 – 8,500 (deluxe rooms) | Smaller property; offers a more intimate feel. |<br />\n<br />\n*All prices are estimates based on typical rates for October–February; exact rates must be confirmed at booking.*  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>FOOD AND EXPERIENCES</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Local cuisine:</strong> Undhiyu (mixed vegetable casserole), Locho, Khaman, Dhokla, Surti Ponk (tender roasted corn), fresh pomfret and prawns at coastal stalls.  <br />\n- <strong>Dining recommendations:</strong>  <br />\n  - *Jalaram Khichdi* – classic Gujarati thali.  <br />\n  - *Gopal Locho* – street‑food specialty.  <br />\n  - *The Grand Bhagwati – Rooftop* – upscale Gujarati fusion.  <br />\n  - *Moti Mahal* – quick bites and snacks.  <br />\n- <strong>Cultural experiences:</strong>  <br />\n  - Evening street‑food crawl in the Old City.  <br />\n  - Attend a short Gujarati folk dance (Garba) performance if a local festival coincides (often held in community halls).  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>ESTIMATED BUDGET</strong> *(per adult, mid‑range assumptions)*  <br />\n<br />\n| Category | Approx. Cost (₹) |<br />\n|----------|-----------------|<br />\n| Accommodation (2 nights) | 20,000 – 30,000 |<br />\n| Transport (airport/railway transfers, intra‑city rides) | 3,000 – 5,000 |<br />\n| Meals (breakfast included, lunch &amp; dinner) | 6,000 – 9,000 |<br />\n| Activities &amp; entry fees (castle, park, beach, workshop) | 1,500 – 2,500 |<br />\n| Miscellaneous (tips, souvenirs) | 2,000 – 3,000 |<br />\n| <strong>Total estimated</strong> | <strong>≈ ₹32,500 – ₹49,500</strong> |<br />\n<br />\n*Assumptions: mid‑range hotels, meals at recommended venues, rideshare rates, and no major shopping splurges.*  <br />\n<br />\n---<br />\n<br />\n<strong>IMPORTANT TRAVEL TIPS</strong>  <br />\n- <strong>Weather &amp; clothing:</strong> Winter (Oct‑Feb) is pleasant (20‑30 °C). Light jackets for evenings; comfortable walking shoes. Summer can exceed 40 °C – avoid if possible.  <br />\n- <strong>Transport:</strong> Uber, Ola, and local auto‑rickshaws are reliable. For day trips (e.g., Dumas Beach) a hired car with driver is convenient.  <br />\n- <strong>Reservations:</strong> Book hotels at least 2 weeks in advance for winter season. Arrange textile‑market and diamond‑workshop tours through the hotel concierge ahead of time.  <br />\n- <strong>Safety:</strong> Surat is generally safe for tourists. Keep an eye on personal belongings in crowded markets. Night travel is fine in well‑lit areas; use rideshare apps.  <br />\n- <strong>Documents:</strong> Carry a government‑issued ID (Aadhaar, passport) for hotel check‑in and any guided tours. No visa is required for Indian citizens; foreign visitors need a valid Indian visa.  <br />\n- <strong>Health:</strong> Stay hydrated; carry bottled water. Street food is delicious but choose stalls with good hygiene. Basic medical facilities are available in the city centre.  <br />\n<br />\nEnjoy your three‑day immersion in Surat’s vibrant culture, historic charm, and coastal breezes!', NULL, '2026-11-20 04:16:04'),
